window.TWG_I18N=window.TWG_I18N||{};TWG_I18N["zh-hant"]=Object.assign(TWG_I18N["zh-hant"]||{},{"I'll build you a tailor-made path to pass your Level 2 exam. It takes 5 quick questions.":"我會為你量身打造一條通過 Level 2 考試的學習路徑，只需回答 5 個簡單問題。","The vine and the grape":"葡萄樹與葡萄","Climate, weather and site":"氣候、天氣與園地","Choices in the vineyard":"葡萄園裡的選擇","Reading the label: origin and rules":"讀懂酒標：產地與法規","Winery choices and ageing":"酒廠的選擇與熟成","Pinot Grigio / Pinot Gris":"灰皮諾（Pinot Grigio / Pinot Gris）","Syrah / Shiraz":"希哈／希拉茲（Syrah / Shiraz）","Label terms: Burgundy, Bordeaux, Alsace, Germany":"酒標術語：布根地、波爾多、阿爾薩斯、德國","Reds of France and Spain":"法國與西班牙的紅酒","Reds of Italy":"義大利的紅酒","New World reds":"新世界的紅酒","Regional whites":"地區性白酒","Sherry":"Sherry","Serving wine":"侍酒","Tasting with a method":"有方法地品飲","From vineyard to winery":"從葡萄園到酒廠","The principal grapes":"主要葡萄品種","Regional grapes":"地區性葡萄品種","r3":"r3","Sparkling and fortified":"氣泡酒與加烈酒","s3":"s3","Service, storage and food":"侍酒、儲存與餐酒搭配","Which part of the grape gives a red wine its colour?":"葡萄的哪個部位讓紅酒有顏色？","The seeds":"葡萄籽","The stems":"果梗","Colour is held in the skins of black grapes; the pulp is almost always pale.":"顏色存在於黑葡萄的果皮中；果肉幾乎都是淺色的。","With very few exceptions, the pulp of white and black grapes is the same pale colour. The skin holds colour and tannin, both much more plentiful in black grapes. So a red wine only gains its colour if the juice stays in contact with the skins; seeds and stems mainly bring tannin, not colour.":"除了極少數例外，白葡萄和黑葡萄的果肉都是同樣的淺色。果皮含有顏色和單寧，而黑葡萄的果皮含量多得多。所以紅酒只有在葡萄汁與果皮保持接觸時才會染上顏色；葡萄籽和果梗主要帶來單寧，而不是顏色。","What is grape pulp mainly made of?":"葡萄果肉主要由什麼組成？","Water and sugar":"水和糖","Colour and flavour":"顏色和風味","Tannin and acids":"單寧和酸","Pulp is mostly water and sugar, with some acids and flavours.":"果肉主要是水和糖，還有一些酸和風味物質。","The pulp is the juicy part of the grape: water and sugar are its main components, along with acids and flavours. Colour and tannin are concentrated in the skin, while seeds and stems are rich in tannin. Knowing what each part contains helps explain how white, rosé and red wines are made.":"果肉是葡萄多汁的部分：主要成分是水和糖，另外還有酸和風味物質。顏色和單寧集中在果皮，而葡萄籽和果梗富含單寧。了解每個部位含有什麼，有助於理解白酒、粉紅酒和紅酒的釀造方式。","Why must seeds and stems be handled gently in the winery?":"為什麼在酒廠裡必須輕柔處理葡萄籽和果梗？","They are high in tannins that can make wine bitter":"它們含有大量單寧，可能讓酒變苦","They contain almost all of the grape's sugar":"它們含有葡萄幾乎所有的糖分","They are the main source of the wine's colour":"它們是葡萄酒顏色的主要來源","They release acids that make the wine too sour":"它們會釋放讓酒過酸的酸","Seeds and stems hold a lot of tannin, which turns bitter if they are handled roughly.":"葡萄籽和果梗含有大量單寧，處理過於粗暴就會變苦。","Seeds and stems contain plenty of tannin, and if they are crushed or worked roughly this passes into the wine and makes it very bitter. Sugar is found in the pulp and colour in the skins of black grapes, so the other answers give seeds and stems a role they do not play.":"葡萄籽和果梗含有大量單寧，如果被壓碎或粗暴處理，單寧就會進入酒中，讓酒非常苦澀。糖存在於果肉，顏色存在於黑葡萄的果皮，所以其他選項賦予了葡萄籽和果梗它們並不具備的作用。","Which process allows the vine to produce sugars?":"哪個過程讓葡萄樹能夠產生糖分？","Photosynthesis":"光合作用","Pollination":"授粉","In photosynthesis, sunlight lets the vine combine CO2 and water into sugars.":"光合作用中，陽光讓葡萄樹把 CO2 和水結合成糖。","The leaves take in carbon dioxide from the air and the roots take up water from the soil. Using sunlight, the vine combines these to make sugars: this is photosynthesis. The sugars fuel the plant's growth and the ripening of the grapes. Véraison, pollination and fruit set are stages in the development of the grape itself.":"葉片從空氣中吸收二氧化碳，根部從土壤中吸收水分。葡萄樹利用陽光把兩者結合成糖：這就是光合作用。這些糖為植株的生長和葡萄的成熟提供能量。轉色期、授粉和著果則是葡萄本身發育的不同階段。","Why does the vine go dormant in winter?":"為什麼葡萄樹在冬天會進入休眠？","There is not enough heat for it to grow":"熱量不足，無法生長","The soil no longer contains nutrients":"土壤中已經沒有養分","The roots stop absorbing CO2":"根部停止吸收 CO2","The plant has just been pruned":"植株剛被修剪過","Without enough heat a vine cannot grow, so in winter it stops.":"沒有足夠的熱量，葡萄樹就無法生長，所以冬天會停止生長。","Heat, supplied by the sun, is one of the vine's five needs. When it is too cold the plant cannot grow and becomes dormant, having dropped its leaves in autumn. CO2 is taken in by the leaves, not the roots, and winter pruning happens precisely because the vine is already dormant.":"由太陽提供的熱量是葡萄樹的五大需求之一。天氣太冷時，植株無法生長而進入休眠，葉子在秋天就已掉落。CO2 是由葉片而不是根部吸收的，而冬季修剪正是因為葡萄樹已經在休眠才進行的。","What does the vine take in through its leaves?":"葡萄樹透過葉片吸收什麼？","Nutrients":"養分","Leaves take in CO2 from the air; water and nutrients come through the roots.":"葉片從空氣中吸收 CO2；水和養分則由根部吸收。","A vine takes what it needs either from the soil through its roots or from the air through its leaves. Carbon dioxide enters through the leaves; water and small amounts of nutrients come in through the roots. Sugars are not absorbed at all: the plant makes them itself by photosynthesis, using light, CO2 and water.":"葡萄樹所需的東西，不是透過根部從土壤中取得，就是透過葉片從空氣中取得。二氧化碳從葉片進入；水和少量養分從根部進入。糖完全不是吸收來的：植株利用光、CO2 和水，透過光合作用自己製造糖。","How are vine flowers pollinated?":"葡萄樹的花是怎麼授粉的？","They pollinate themselves":"自花授粉","By bees":"靠蜜蜂","By birds":"靠鳥類","By hand, by the grower":"由種植者人工授粉","Vines are self-pollinating, so they do not need showy flowers to attract insects.":"葡萄樹會自花授粉，所以不需要鮮豔的花朵來吸引昆蟲。","Many plants have colourful flowers to attract pollinating insects. Vines do not: their flowers pollinate themselves. Each pollinated flower can then grow seeds and swell, becoming a grape at fruit set. That is why vine flowers are small and inconspicuous.":"許多植物有色彩鮮豔的花朵來吸引授粉昆蟲。葡萄樹不需要：它的花會自花授粉。每朵授粉的花接著就能長出種子並膨大，在著果時成為一顆葡萄。這就是為什麼葡萄樹的花又小又不顯眼。","What is the stage called when the pollinated flower swells into a grape?":"授粉後的花膨大成葡萄的階段叫什麼？","Extra-ripening":"過熟","At fruit set the flower grows seeds, swells and becomes a small green grape.":"著果時，花朵長出種子、膨大，變成一顆綠色小葡萄。","The order is: flowering in spring, fruit set when the pollinated flower starts to grow seeds and swell, then summer growth, véraison in mid-summer and finally ripening. Newly set grapes are small, hard, green and unpleasant; they still need to grow and ripen to become wine grapes.":"順序是：春天開花，授粉的花開始長出種子並膨大時為著果，接著是夏季生長、盛夏的轉色期，最後是成熟。剛著果的葡萄又小又硬、呈綠色且難吃；它們還需要長大、成熟，才能成為釀酒葡萄。","What happens at véraison?":"轉色期會發生什麼？","Grapes lose their green colour and ripening begins":"葡萄褪去綠色，開始成熟","Flowers are pollinated and start forming seeds":"花朵授粉並開始形成種子","The vine drops its leaves and goes dormant":"葡萄樹落葉並進入休眠","Grapes shrivel and turn into raisins":"葡萄乾縮變成葡萄乾","Véraison marks the start of ripening, when grapes change colour.":"轉色期標誌著成熟的開始，葡萄在這時改變顏色。","By mid-summer the grapes are big enough for the vine to start ripening them. Véraison is when they lose their green colour: white grapes turn golden, black grapes go red and then purple. Pollination happens much earlier, leaf fall comes in autumn, and shrivelling only occurs if picking is delayed a long time.":"到了盛夏，葡萄已經長得夠大，葡萄樹開始讓它們成熟。轉色期就是葡萄褪去綠色的時候：白葡萄轉為金黃色，黑葡萄先變紅再變紫。授粉發生得早得多，落葉在秋天，而乾縮只有在採收大幅延後時才會出現。","What colour do black grapes turn during véraison?":"黑葡萄在轉色期會變成什麼顏色？","Red, then purple":"先紅後紫","Golden, then red":"先金黃後紅","Purple, then red":"先紫後紅","Yellow, then brown":"先黃後褐","At véraison black grapes go from green to red and then purple.":"轉色期時，黑葡萄從綠色變成紅色，再變成紫色。","Véraison is the colour change that opens the ripening period. White grapes go from green to golden, while black grapes first turn red and then purple. The colour sits in the skin, which is exactly where a red wine gets its hue during winemaking.":"轉色期是開啟成熟期的顏色變化。白葡萄從綠色轉為金黃色，黑葡萄則先轉紅再轉紫。顏色存在於果皮中，而紅酒在釀造過程中正是從果皮獲得色澤。","How do acidity and sugar change during ripening?":"成熟過程中，酸度和糖分如何變化？","Acidity falls and sugar rises":"酸度下降，糖分上升","Acidity rises and sugar falls":"酸度上升，糖分下降","Both rise":"兩者都上升","Both fall":"兩者都下降","As grapes ripen they lose acidity and build up sugar.":"葡萄成熟時會失去酸度並累積糖分。","Unripe grapes are very acidic with hardly any sugar. As they ripen, they swell with water, acidity drops and sugar rises, while herbaceous notes give way to the variety's signature flavours. Only with extra-ripeness and shrivelling do acids and sugars become concentrated together, because water evaporates.":"未成熟的葡萄非常酸，幾乎沒有糖分。隨著成熟，葡萄吸水膨大，酸度下降、糖分上升，草本氣息也逐漸讓位給品種的招牌風味。只有在過熟和乾縮時，由於水分蒸發，酸和糖才會一起濃縮。","A black grape is picked with unripe tannins. Which fault is most likely in the wine?":"一批黑葡萄在單寧尚未成熟時採收。酒中最可能出現哪種缺點？","Bitterness":"苦味","Excessive sweetness":"過甜","Dried-fruit aromas":"乾果香氣","Overly deep colour":"顏色過深","Unripe tannins can make a red wine taste bitter.":"未成熟的單寧可能讓紅酒嚐起來有苦味。","During ripening, along with sugar and flavours, the tannins in black grape skins also ripen. Tannins shape the mouthfeel of red wines, but unripe tannins taste bitter. So the grower must time the harvest by checking not just the sugar level but also how ripe the tannins are.":"成熟過程中，除了糖分和風味，黑葡萄果皮中的單寧也會成熟。單寧塑造紅酒的口感，但未成熟的單寧嚐起來是苦的。所以種植者決定採收時機時，不只要檢查糖分，也要檢查單寧的成熟度。","In some white grapes, how do aromas develop as ripeness increases?":"對某些白葡萄來說，隨著成熟度提高，香氣如何發展？","From green fruit to stone fruit to tropical fruit":"從綠色水果到核果再到熱帶水果","From tropical fruit to stone fruit to green fruit":"從熱帶水果到核果再到綠色水果","From fresh fruit to cooked fruit":"從新鮮水果到煮熟的水果","From dried fruit to fresh fruit":"從乾果到新鮮水果","The riper a white grape gets, the more its aromas move from green to stone to tropical fruit.":"白葡萄越成熟，香氣就越從綠色水果轉向核果，再轉向熱帶水果。","As grapes ripen, herbaceous notes fade and varietal flavours appear. For some white grapes the typical path is green fruit, then stone fruit, then tropical fruit. The shift from fresh to cooked fruit describes black grapes instead, while dried-fruit aromas only come with extra-ripeness.":"葡萄成熟時，草本氣息減弱，品種風味出現。對某些白葡萄來說，典型的路徑是綠色水果、核果，然後是熱帶水果。從新鮮水果到煮熟水果描述的是黑葡萄，而乾果香氣只在過熟時才會出現。","Why is dry weather needed to leave grapes on the vine beyond the normal harvest?":"為什麼要把葡萄留在樹上超過正常採收期，必須有乾燥的天氣？","Rain can lead to fungal diseases":"下雨可能引發真菌病害","Rain makes acidity rise too much":"下雨會讓酸度上升太多","Rain makes the skins darker":"下雨會讓果皮顏色變深","Rain stops photosynthesis":"下雨會中止光合作用","Rain brings moisture that encourages fungi which can spoil the grapes.":"下雨帶來濕氣，助長可能破壞葡萄的真菌。","For extra-ripening the weather must stay dry, because rain encourages fungal diseases, and warm enough for ripening to carry on. Under these conditions aromas become riper, sugar rises and, over time, the grapes shrivel, concentrating sugars and acids: ideal fruit for sweet wines.":"要讓葡萄過熟，天氣必須保持乾燥，因為下雨會助長真菌病害；也必須夠溫暖，讓成熟得以持續。在這樣的條件下，香氣變得更成熟、糖分上升，久而久之葡萄乾縮，糖和酸隨之濃縮：這是釀造甜酒的理想果實。","A grape left on the vine for a long time shrivels. Which aromas does it tend to develop?":"一顆葡萄在樹上留了很久而乾縮。它傾向於發展出哪種香氣？","Dried fruit":"乾果","Herbaceous":"草本","Green fruit":"綠色水果","Fresh floral":"清新花香","As the grapes shrivel, water evaporates and dried-fruit aromas appear.":"葡萄乾縮時水分蒸發，乾果香氣隨之出現。","In the early stages of extra-ripeness, aromas become very ripe and sugar rises. If the grapes stay on the vine longer, water evaporates and they turn almost into raisins: acids and sugars concentrate and dried-fruit aromas develop. Herbaceous and green-fruit notes, by contrast, are typical of unripe grapes.":"在過熟的初期，香氣變得非常成熟，糖分上升。如果葡萄在樹上留得更久，水分蒸發，它們幾乎變成葡萄乾：酸和糖濃縮，發展出乾果香氣。相反地，草本和綠色水果的氣息是未成熟葡萄的典型特徵。","Which of these is NOT one of the five things a vine needs?":"下列哪一項不是葡萄樹的五大需求之一？","Insects to pollinate its flowers":"為花朵授粉的昆蟲","Warmth":"溫暖","Carbon dioxide taken from the air by the leaves":"葉片從空氣中吸收的二氧化碳","Vines pollinate themselves: they need warmth, sunlight, carbon dioxide, water and nutrients, not insects.":"葡萄樹會自花授粉：它需要溫暖、陽光、二氧化碳、水和養分，而不需要昆蟲。","A vine's five needs are warmth, sunlight, carbon dioxide, water and nutrients, so warmth, CO2 and nutrients are all essential. Unlike many plants with bright flowers, the vine does not need to attract insects, because its flowers pollinate themselves.":"葡萄樹的五大需求是溫暖、陽光、二氧化碳、水和養分，所以溫暖、CO2 和養分都不可或缺。不同於許多花朵鮮豔的植物，葡萄樹不需要吸引昆蟲，因為它的花會自花授粉。","Through which part does the vine take up water and nutrients?":"葡萄樹透過哪個部位吸收水和養分？","The roots":"根部","The leaves":"葉片","The flowers, during spring":"春天時的花朵","The skins of the ripening grapes":"成熟中的葡萄果皮","Water and nutrients come from the soil and are taken up by the roots.":"水和養分來自土壤，由根部吸收。","Because it is rooted to the ground, the vine takes what it needs either from the soil, through its roots, or from the air, through its leaves. The leaves take in carbon dioxide, not water. Flowers and grape skins play no part in this.":"由於扎根於地面，葡萄樹所需的東西不是透過根部從土壤中取得，就是透過葉片從空氣中取得。葉片吸收的是二氧化碳，不是水。花朵和葡萄果皮在這方面都不起作用。","What does the vine use the sugars made by photosynthesis for?":"葡萄樹用光合作用產生的糖來做什麼？","To power its growth and ripen its grapes":"為生長提供能量，並讓葡萄成熟","To protect itself from frost during winter dormancy":"在冬季休眠期保護自己免受霜害","To attract insects to its flowers":"吸引昆蟲到花朵上","To make tannins in the seeds":"在葡萄籽中製造單寧","Sugars from photosynthesis fuel the plant's growth and the ripening of its grapes.":"光合作用產生的糖為植株生長和葡萄成熟提供能量。","Sunlight lets the vine combine CO2 and water into sugars, which are its source of energy. In winter the vine is dormant because there is not enough heat, not because it uses sugar against frost. It has no need to attract insects, since it pollinates itself.":"陽光讓葡萄樹把 CO2 和水結合成糖，這是它的能量來源。葡萄樹冬天休眠是因為熱量不足，而不是因為用糖來抵抗霜凍。它也不需要吸引昆蟲，因為它會自花授粉。","How long can a vine live?":"葡萄樹可以活多久？","60 years or more":"60 年或更久","A single growing season":"只有一個生長季","About 5 years, then it must be replaced":"大約 5 年，之後就必須更換","No more than 15–20 years in most vineyards":"在多數葡萄園裡不超過 15–20 年","The vine is a long-lived plant that can live for 60 years or more, repeating the same cycle every year.":"葡萄樹是長壽的植物，可以活 60 年或更久，每年重複同樣的週期。","The vine is not an annual plant: each spring it starts again from the same trunk. This long life is what makes 'old vines' possible, prized for the quality of their grapes. The other lifespans offered are far too short.":"葡萄樹不是一年生植物：每年春天都從同一根主幹重新開始。正是這種長壽造就了備受珍視、葡萄品質出眾的「老藤」。其他選項的壽命都太短了。","Which description of the vine's yearly cycle is correct?":"下列哪一項對葡萄樹年度週期的描述是正確的？","Shoots and flowers in spring, ripe grapes by late summer, leaves dropping in autumn":"春天長出新梢和花朵，夏末葡萄成熟，秋天落葉","Flowers in winter, fruit in spring, dormancy in summer":"冬天開花，春天結果，夏天休眠","Leaves dropping in spring, flowers in summer and grapes ripe only in the middle of winter":"春天落葉，夏天開花，直到隆冬葡萄才成熟","Continuous growth all year, with no real pause":"全年持續生長，沒有真正的停頓","The growing season runs from spring to autumn; in winter the vine rests.":"生長季從春天持續到秋天；冬天葡萄樹休息。","In spring the vine grows shoots, leaves and flowers; by late summer the flowers have become ripe grapes. Leaf fall in autumn ends the season, and in winter the plant is dormant because it is too cold to grow. Year-round growth is therefore impossible.":"春天葡萄樹長出新梢、葉子和花朵；到了夏末，花朵已經變成成熟的葡萄。秋天落葉結束這一季，冬天植株因為太冷無法生長而休眠。所以全年生長是不可能的。","Riesling and Cabernet Sauvignon differ greatly in colour and flavour. What are they, botanically?":"麗絲玲和卡本內蘇維濃在顏色和風味上差異很大。從植物學上看，它們是什麼？","Two varieties of the same European species":"同一個歐洲物種的兩個品種","Two different species, one European and one American":"兩個不同物種，一個是歐洲種，一個是美洲種","Two wild species gathered in nature":"在野外採集的兩個野生物種","Two recent crosses between North American and Asian species":"北美與亞洲物種的兩個近期雜交種","Almost all wine comes from one European species, which exists in many different varieties.":"幾乎所有葡萄酒都來自同一個歐洲物種，它有許多不同的品種。","There are several vine species native to Eurasia or North America, but wine is almost always made from the European one. Its varieties differ in the look of the grapes, their taste and their flavours. Wine grapes are not gathered from the wild either: they are grown in carefully managed vineyards.":"原生於歐亞大陸或北美洲的葡萄屬物種有好幾種，但葡萄酒幾乎都是用歐洲種釀造的。它的各個品種在葡萄外觀、味道和風味上各不相同。釀酒葡萄也不是從野外採集的：它們種植在精心管理的葡萄園裡。","What does each cluster of vine flowers become?":"葡萄樹的每一串花會變成什麼？","A bunch of grapes":"一串葡萄","A new shoot for the following year":"來年的一根新梢","One single, very large grape":"一顆非常大的葡萄","A leaf, while the single flowers become grapes":"一片葉子，而單朵花才會變成葡萄","Each flower cluster becomes a bunch of grapes; each pollinated flower becomes one grape.":"每一串花會變成一串葡萄；每一朵授粉的花會變成一顆葡萄。","In spring the vine produces clusters of flowers. Each individual flower, once pollinated, grows seeds and swells into a grape, and together they form the bunch. That is why poor flowering directly reduces the crop.":"春天葡萄樹長出一串串花。每一朵花授粉後長出種子並膨大成一顆葡萄，合起來就成了一串葡萄。這就是為什麼開花不良會直接減少收成。","What is the correct order of the stages of grape formation?":"葡萄形成各階段的正確順序是什麼？","Flowering, fruit set, véraison, ripening":"開花、著果、轉色期、成熟","Fruit set, flowering, ripening, véraison":"著果、開花、成熟、轉色期","Flowering, véraison, fruit set, ripening":"開花、轉色期、著果、成熟","Véraison, flowering, ripening and finally fruit set":"轉色期、開花、成熟，最後著果","First the flower, then the green grape (fruit set), then the colour change (véraison) that starts ripening.":"先是花，然後是綠色的葡萄（著果），接著是開啟成熟的顏色變化（轉色期）。","The vine flowers in spring, and the pollinated flower becomes a small, hard, green grape. In mid-summer véraison marks the start of ripening, which continues until harvest. Véraison cannot come before fruit set: without a grape there is nothing to change colour.":"葡萄樹在春天開花，授粉的花變成一顆又小又硬的綠色葡萄。盛夏時，轉色期標誌著成熟的開始，成熟一直持續到採收。轉色期不可能在著果之前：沒有葡萄，就沒有東西可以變色。","What colour do white grapes turn at véraison?":"白葡萄在轉色期會變成什麼顏色？","Golden":"金黃色","Dark green":"深綠色","Brown, like a raisin":"像葡萄乾一樣的褐色","At véraison grapes lose their green: white grapes turn golden, black grapes red and then purple.":"轉色期時葡萄褪去綠色：白葡萄轉為金黃色，黑葡萄先變紅再變紫。","Véraison happens in mid-summer and marks the start of ripening. The red-then-purple change applies to black grapes, not white ones. A brown, shrivelled look only appears much later, if grapes stay on the vine until they turn into raisins.":"轉色期發生在盛夏，標誌著成熟的開始。先紅後紫的變化是黑葡萄的，不是白葡萄的。褐色、乾縮的外觀要晚得多才會出現，只有當葡萄留在樹上直到變成葡萄乾時才會這樣。","At the start of ripening, what is a grape like?":"成熟剛開始時，葡萄是什麼樣子？","Very acidic, with hardly any sugar and a herbaceous taste":"非常酸，幾乎沒有糖分，帶有草本味道","Sweet, low in acid, with tropical fruit aromas":"甜、低酸，帶有熱帶水果香氣","Soft and juicy, already showing its signature aromas":"柔軟多汁，已經展現出招牌香氣","High in sugar, but with tannins still unripe in the pulp":"糖分高，但果肉中的單寧仍未成熟","Before ripening, the grape is very acidic, low in sugar and has an unattractive herbaceous taste.":"成熟之前，葡萄非常酸、糖分低，還帶有不討喜的草本味道。","During ripening the grape swells with water and softens, acidity falls, sugar rises and herbaceous notes give way to the variety's signature aromas. Sweetness and tropical fruit therefore belong to a ripe grape, not the start of ripening. Tannins, meanwhile, are in the skin, not the pulp.":"成熟過程中，葡萄吸水膨大並變軟，酸度下降，糖分上升，草本氣息讓位給品種的招牌香氣。所以甜味和熱帶水果屬於成熟的葡萄，而不是成熟剛開始時。至於單寧，它存在於果皮，而不是果肉。","As a black grape ripens, how do its aromas change?":"黑葡萄成熟時，香氣如何變化？","From tropical fruit to green fruit":"從熱帶水果到綠色水果","From cooked fruit to fresh fruit":"從煮熟的水果到新鮮水果","From vanilla and coconut to crunchy red fruit":"從香草和椰子到爽脆的紅色水果","In black grapes, rising ripeness moves the flavours from fresh fruit towards cooked fruit.":"對黑葡萄來說，成熟度提高會讓風味從新鮮水果轉向煮熟的水果。","The green-to-stone-to-tropical sequence applies to some white grapes, and runs in that direction, not the reverse. Vanilla and coconut come from new oak, not from the grape. For black grapes, the marker is the move from fresh to cooked fruit.":"綠色水果到核果再到熱帶水果的順序適用於某些白葡萄，而且是這個方向，不是相反。香草和椰子來自新橡木桶，不是來自葡萄。對黑葡萄來說，指標是從新鮮水果轉向煮熟的水果。","What do tannins contribute to a red wine?":"單寧為紅酒帶來什麼？","To its mouthfeel":"口感","To its red colour, which comes entirely from the tannins in the seeds":"紅色，完全來自葡萄籽中的單寧","To its sweetness":"甜味","To its alcohol level":"酒精濃度","Tannins from black grape skins give red wines their mouthfeel.":"來自黑葡萄果皮的單寧賦予紅酒口感。","Tannins are compounds in the skins of black grapes (and also in seeds and stems), and they ripen during the ripening period. Colour comes from skin pigments, not seeds. Sweetness and alcohol depend on sugar, not on tannin.":"單寧是存在於黑葡萄果皮（以及葡萄籽和果梗）中的化合物，會在成熟期間逐漸成熟。顏色來自果皮的色素，不是葡萄籽。甜味和酒精取決於糖分，與單寧無關。","Why does a grape left on the vine until it shrivels have more concentrated sugars and acids?":"為什麼留在樹上直到乾縮的葡萄，糖和酸會更濃縮？","Because the water in the grape evaporates":"因為葡萄中的水分蒸發了","Because a fungus pierces the skin":"因為真菌刺穿了果皮","Because the water freezes inside the grape":"因為葡萄裡的水結冰了","Because the vine keeps pumping sugar and acid into the grapes even after its leaves have fallen":"因為即使葉子掉光，葡萄樹仍持續把糖和酸送進葡萄","With a long hang time the water evaporates and the grape becomes a raisin, concentrating sugars and acids.":"長時間掛在樹上，水分蒸發，葡萄變成葡萄乾，糖和酸隨之濃縮。","This is raisining on the vine, which also brings dried-fruit aromas. The fungus that pierces the skin is Botrytis (noble rot) and freezing the water is how icewine is made: two other ways of concentrating sugar. A vine with no leaves can no longer make sugar by photosynthesis.":"這就是在樹上風乾成葡萄乾，同時也會帶來乾果香氣。刺穿果皮的真菌是貴腐菌（Botrytis），而讓水結冰是冰酒的釀造方式：這是另外兩種濃縮糖分的方法。沒有葉子的葡萄樹已經無法透過光合作用製造糖。","In the early stages of extra-ripeness, what happens to the grapes?":"在過熟的初期，葡萄會發生什麼？","They develop exaggerated ripe aromas and build up more sugar":"發展出誇張的成熟香氣，累積更多糖分","They lose sugar and regain herbaceous notes":"失去糖分，重新出現草本氣息","They shrivel at once and taste of dried fruit":"立刻乾縮，嚐起來有乾果味","They turn green and hard again, as just after fruit set":"重新變綠變硬，就像剛著果時一樣","Early extra-ripeness exaggerates ripe aromas and increases sugar; shrivelling only comes later.":"過熟初期會放大成熟香氣並提高糖分；乾縮要晚一點才會出現。","If grapes stay on the vine past the normal harvest, in dry and warm enough weather, they keep developing. Only after a longer period does water evaporate, the grapes shrivel and dried-fruit notes appear. Herbaceous notes belong to unripe grapes.":"如果葡萄在正常採收期之後仍留在樹上，而天氣夠乾燥、夠溫暖，它們會繼續發展。要再過較長一段時間，水分才會蒸發，葡萄乾縮，出現乾果氣息。草本氣息則屬於未成熟的葡萄。","Where in the grape are flavours most concentrated?":"葡萄的風味最集中在哪裡？","In the skin and just beneath it":"果皮及其正下方","In the seeds":"葡萄籽","In the stem holding the bunch":"支撐果串的果梗","At the centre of the pulp, far from the skin, where there is most water":"果肉中心，遠離果皮、水分最多的地方","The skin and the area immediately below it hold high levels of flavour.":"果皮及其正下方的區域含有大量風味物質。","The pulp also contains acids and flavours, but it is mostly water and sugar. Seeds and stems are known for tannins, which can turn bitter if handled roughly. This is why contact with the skins matters so much to a wine's flavour.":"果肉也含有酸和風味物質，但主要是水和糖。葡萄籽和果梗以單寧著稱，處理粗暴時可能變苦。這就是為什麼與果皮的接觸對葡萄酒的風味如此重要。","Which parts of the grape and bunch contain tannins?":"葡萄和果串的哪些部位含有單寧？","Skins, seeds and stems":"果皮、葡萄籽和果梗","Only the pulp":"只有果肉","Pulp and juice, but never the skin or seeds":"果肉和果汁，但絕不在果皮或葡萄籽中","Only the stems":"只有果梗","Tannins are in the skins, especially of black grapes, and at high levels in seeds and stems.":"單寧存在於果皮中（尤其是黑葡萄），在葡萄籽和果梗中的含量也很高。","The pulp is mainly water, sugar, acids and flavours, not tannin. Tannins from black skins give red wines their structure, while those from seeds and stems can make wine bitter if crushed roughly. That is why winemakers handle them gently.":"果肉主要是水、糖、酸和風味物質，不是單寧。黑葡萄果皮的單寧賦予紅酒結構，而葡萄籽和果梗的單寧若被粗暴壓碎，可能讓酒變苦。所以釀酒師會輕柔地處理它們。","Climate is the long-term average, weather is what happens day to day":"氣候是長期平均，天氣是每天發生的狀況","Climate changes every year, weather stays stable for decades":"氣候每年都在變，天氣則數十年保持穩定","Climate covers only rainfall, weather only temperature":"氣候只涵蓋降雨，天氣只涵蓋溫度","Climate refers to one vineyard, weather to a whole country":"氣候指的是一座葡萄園，天氣指的是整個國家","Climate is the long-term average pattern; weather is what actually happens each day.":"氣候是長期的平均模式；天氣是每天實際發生的狀況。","Climate describes the average levels of temperature, sunlight and rainfall a region can expect; it does not change from year to year, though it can shift over decades. Weather is what actually happens day to day: cool or hot vintages, frost, hail and sudden downpours are all matters of weather.":"氣候描述的是一個產區可預期的平均溫度、日照和降雨水準；它不會年年改變，但可能在數十年間轉變。天氣則是每天實際發生的事：涼爽或炎熱的年份、霜凍、冰雹和突如其來的大雨，都屬於天氣。","A region has an average growing season temperature of 15.5°C. How is its climate classified?":"某產區生長季的平均溫度為 15.5°C。它的氣候屬於哪一類？","An average growing season temperature of 16.5°C or below counts as cool.":"生長季平均溫度在 16.5°C 以下屬於涼爽氣候。","The three bands used are: cool, 16.5°C (62°F) or below; moderate, 16.5 to 18.5°C (62 to 65°F); warm, 18.5 to 21°C (65 to 70°F). At 15.5°C the region is below the 16.5°C threshold, so its climate is cool. Such a climate tends to give grapes with higher acidity and less-ripe flavours.":"使用的三個區間是：涼爽，16.5°C（62°F）以下；溫和，16.5 至 18.5°C（62 至 65°F）；溫暖，18.5 至 21°C（65 至 70°F）。15.5°C 低於 16.5°C 的門檻，所以這個產區屬於涼爽氣候。這樣的氣候往往讓葡萄酸度較高、風味較不成熟。","When does the growing season run in the southern hemisphere?":"南半球的生長季在什麼時候？","January to June":"1 月到 6 月","July to December":"7 月到 12 月","In the southern hemisphere the season runs October to April, the reverse of the north.":"南半球的生長季是 10 月到 4 月，與北半球相反。","Seasons are reversed between the two hemispheres. In the northern hemisphere the growing season runs from April to October; in the southern hemisphere from October to April. That is why the Australian harvest happens early in the calendar year, while California's comes towards the end.":"南北半球的季節相反。北半球的生長季從 4 月到 10 月；南半球則從 10 月到 4 月。這就是為什麼澳洲在年初採收，而加州的採收接近年底。","Which grape is given as an example of a variety that only ripens well in warm climates?":"哪個品種被舉例為只有在溫暖氣候才能好好成熟的品種？","Grenache can only grow and ripen successfully in warm climates.":"格那希只能在溫暖氣候中順利生長和成熟。","Temperature decides which varieties can grow in a region. Grenache is the example of a grape that needs a warm climate to ripen. Chardonnay is the opposite example: it grows well in a range of climates but develops different flavours depending on the heat available.":"溫度決定了一個產區能種哪些品種。格那希是需要溫暖氣候才能成熟的例子。夏多內則是相反的例子：它在各種氣候中都長得很好，但會依可得的熱量發展出不同的風味。","What is the most important factor influencing a wine region's climate?":"影響葡萄酒產區氣候最重要的因素是什麼？","Soil type":"土壤類型","Nearness to a river":"鄰近河流","Slope aspect":"坡向","Latitude is the main factor: the closer to the equator, the hotter.":"緯度是主要因素：越接近赤道越熱。","The closer a region is to the equator, the hotter it tends to be. That is why most vineyards lie between 30° and 50° north or south: outside this band it is usually too hot or too cold. Soil, rivers and aspect can then modify the climate of an area or a single vineyard.":"產區越接近赤道，往往越熱。這就是為什麼大多數葡萄園位於南北緯 30° 到 50° 之間：在這個範圍之外通常太熱或太冷。土壤、河流和坡向則可以調節一個地區或單一葡萄園的氣候。","Between which latitudes are most vineyards found?":"大多數葡萄園位於哪兩個緯度之間？","Between 30° and 50° north or south":"南北緯 30° 到 50° 之間","Between 10° and 30° north or south":"南北緯 10° 到 30° 之間","Between 40° and 60° north or south":"南北緯 40° 到 60° 之間","Between 0° and 20° north or south":"南北緯 0° 到 20° 之間","Nearly all vineyards lie between 30° and 50° latitude in both hemispheres.":"幾乎所有葡萄園都位於南北半球緯度 30° 到 50° 之間。","The band between 30° and 50° latitude, north and south of the equator, offers temperatures suited to vines. Closer to the equator it is usually too hot, and further away too cold, for vines to survive. Within the band, altitude, seas, mountains and aspect fine-tune the local climate.":"赤道南北緯度 30° 到 50° 之間的地帶，提供了適合葡萄樹的溫度。越接近赤道通常太熱，越遠離則太冷，葡萄樹難以存活。在這個地帶內，海拔、海洋、山脈和坡向會微調當地氣候。","Two vineyards are at the same latitude, but one is much higher. What should you expect of the higher vineyard?":"兩座葡萄園位於同一緯度，但其中一座海拔高得多。你可以預期海拔較高的葡萄園會怎樣？","A cooler climate":"氣候較涼爽","A warmer climate":"氣候較溫暖","The same climate":"氣候相同","More summer rain":"夏季雨量較多","Temperature drops with altitude, so the higher vineyard is cooler.":"溫度隨海拔升高而下降，所以海拔較高的葡萄園較涼爽。","At the same latitude, a higher vineyard always has a cooler climate. This slows ripening: grapes tend to keep more acidity and build up sugar more slowly. Altitude is therefore a way to make fresher wines even in regions that would be warm because of their latitude.":"在同一緯度上，海拔較高的葡萄園氣候一定較涼爽。這會減緩成熟：葡萄往往保留較多酸度，糖分累積也較慢。因此，即使在因緯度而偏溫暖的產區，海拔也是釀出較清爽葡萄酒的一種方式。","Why does a vineyard on a slope facing the equator produce riper grapes?":"為什麼面向赤道的坡地葡萄園能產出較成熟的葡萄？","It receives more heat and light":"它接收到更多熱量和光照","It receives more rain":"它接收到更多雨水","It has more nutrient-rich soils":"它的土壤養分更豐富","It is more exposed to fog":"它更容易受霧氣影響","A slope facing the equator gets more heat and light, so grapes ripen more.":"面向赤道的坡地接收到更多熱量和光照，所以葡萄更成熟。","Far from the equator, light and heat are scarce and ripening grapes is hard. Planting on a slope facing the equator increases the heat and light reaching the vines. The result is riper grapes than those from a vineyard on flat land or on a slope facing the other way.":"在遠離赤道的地方，光照和熱量都很稀少，葡萄很難成熟。種在面向赤道的坡地上，可以增加葡萄樹接收到的熱量和光照。結果是葡萄比平地或背向坡地的葡萄園更成熟。","What effect do cold ocean currents have on the vineyards of the Cape in South Africa?":"寒冷洋流對南非 Cape 產區的葡萄園有什麼影響？","They cool a warm climate":"為溫暖的氣候降溫","They warm a cool climate":"讓涼爽的氣候變暖","They increase summer rainfall":"增加夏季降雨","They encourage noble rot":"促進貴腐菌生長","Cold currents moderate the Cape's warm climate by cooling it.":"寒冷洋流讓 Cape 溫暖的氣候變得涼爽而溫和。","Warm regions close to the sea can benefit from a moderating influence. In the Cape's grape-growing areas, the climate is cooled by cold ocean currents. The opposite happens in northern Europe, where warm currents warm the vineyards. Breezes blowing in from cold seas also cool coastal areas.":"靠近海洋的溫暖產區可以受益於海洋的調節作用。在 Cape 的葡萄種植區，氣候受到寒冷洋流的冷卻。北歐則相反，溫暖的洋流讓葡萄園變暖。從寒冷海面吹來的微風也會讓沿海地區降溫。","In a cool region, how does a river near the vineyard help?":"在涼爽產區，葡萄園附近的河流有什麼幫助？","It gives warmth, protects from frost and extends ripening":"提供溫暖、防止霜害並延長成熟期","It cools the vineyard and lowers sugar levels":"讓葡萄園降溫並降低糖分","It blocks light and slows photosynthesis":"遮擋光線並減緩光合作用","It shelters the vineyard from cloud and rain":"為葡萄園遮擋雲層和雨水","Rivers hold warmth in autumn, protect against frost and extend the ripening period.":"河流在秋天保有溫暖，防止霜害並延長成熟期。","Rivers warm up and cool down more slowly than land, so in autumn they are warmer than the ground around them. In cool regions they provide warmth, help prevent frost and extend the period warm enough to ripen grapes. They also reflect sunlight. Sheltering vineyards from cloud and rain is the role of mountains, not rivers.":"河流升溫和降溫都比陸地慢，所以秋天時比周圍的土地溫暖。在涼爽產區，河流提供溫暖，有助於防止霜害，並延長足以讓葡萄成熟的溫暖期。河流也會反射陽光。為葡萄園遮擋雲層和雨水是山脈的作用，不是河流。","In which areas is fog an important cooling influence?":"霧氣在哪些地區是重要的降溫因素？","Coastal California and Chile":"加州和智利的沿海地區","Warm regions of Australia":"澳洲的溫暖產區","The Cape regions of South Africa":"南非的 Cape 產區","Northern European vineyards":"北歐的葡萄園","Fog forms at ground level and cools coastal California and Chile.":"霧氣在地面形成，讓加州和智利的沿海地區降溫。","Fog is water vapour that forms at ground level and cools the vineyard; it is a very important moderating influence in coastal California and Chile. In some warmer Australian regions, cloud cover matters instead by reducing sunlight, while at the Cape the key factor is cold ocean currents.":"霧是在地面形成的水氣，會讓葡萄園降溫；它在加州和智利沿海地區是非常重要的調節因素。在澳洲某些較溫暖的產區，重要的反而是減少日照的雲層，而在 Cape，關鍵因素是寒冷洋流。","How can stones on the soil surface help ripening?":"土壤表面的石頭如何幫助成熟？","They absorb heat and warm the vineyard":"吸收熱量，讓葡萄園變暖","They hold more water for the vine":"為葡萄樹保存更多水分","They add nutrients to the soil":"為土壤增添養分","They shelter the vines from wind":"為葡萄樹擋風","Stones absorb heat and make the vineyard warmer, which helps ripening.":"石頭吸收熱量讓葡萄園變暖，有助於成熟。","Soil supplies water and nutrients, but it can also affect vineyard temperature. When the surface is covered in stones, they absorb heat and make the vineyard warmer. That extra heat can help grapes ripen, which is especially useful where the climate struggles to deliver full ripeness.":"土壤提供水和養分，但也可能影響葡萄園的溫度。當地表覆蓋著石頭時，石頭會吸收熱量，讓葡萄園變暖。這些額外的熱量有助於葡萄成熟，在氣候難以讓葡萄完全成熟的地方特別有用。","What typically happens to grapes in a cooler-than-normal vintage?":"在比平常涼爽的年份，葡萄通常會怎樣？","Acidity too high and sugar too low":"酸度太高，糖分太低","Acidity too low and sugar too high":"酸度太低，糖分太高","Dried-fruit aromas and sunburn":"乾果香氣和日灼","Swollen grapes with diluted flavours":"葡萄膨脹，風味被稀釋","With little heat and light, grapes struggle to ripen and stay acidic and low in sugar.":"熱量和光照不足時，葡萄難以成熟，維持高酸低糖。","In a cool vintage temperatures are lower and sunlight less bright than usual, so the vine struggles to ripen its grapes. Acidity stays too high, sugar too low and the variety's signature aromas may not develop. Dried-fruit aromas and sunburn point instead to a very hot vintage.":"在涼爽的年份，溫度比平常低、陽光也不如平常強，葡萄樹難以讓葡萄成熟。酸度維持太高，糖分太低，品種的招牌香氣也可能發展不出來。乾果香氣和日灼則指向非常炎熱的年份。","Why can heavy rain just before harvest reduce grape quality?":"為什麼採收前的大雨會降低葡萄品質？","Grapes swell with water and flavours are diluted":"葡萄吸水膨脹，風味被稀釋","Grapes dry out and turn into raisins":"葡萄乾掉變成葡萄乾","The skins become too dark":"果皮變得太深色","The vine immediately goes dormant":"葡萄樹立刻進入休眠","Excess water in the soil makes the grapes swell, diluting their flavours.":"土壤中過多的水分讓葡萄膨脹，稀釋了風味。","Heavy rain causes two problems. The moisture helps fungal diseases spread, which can reduce both the quantity and quality of grapes. And if heavy rain falls close to harvest, the excess water in the soil makes the grapes swell and dilutes their flavours, so the wine may be less concentrated.":"大雨會造成兩個問題。濕氣助長真菌病害蔓延，可能同時降低葡萄的產量和品質。而如果大雨落在採收前不久，土壤中過多的水分會讓葡萄膨脹、稀釋風味，酒就可能比較不濃郁。","Why are spring frosts particularly dangerous for vines?":"為什麼春霜對葡萄樹特別危險？","They damage new growth and reduce the crop":"它會損害新生枝葉，減少收成","They shrivel grapes that are already ripe":"它會讓已經成熟的葡萄乾縮","They dilute the flavours of the grapes":"它會稀釋葡萄的風味","They cause sunburn on the skins":"它會讓果皮日灼","In spring, frost kills new shoots, so there will be fewer bunches.":"春天的霜凍會凍死新梢，所以果串會變少。","In spring the vine is producing shoots, leaves and flowers. A frost at this point can damage or kill the new growth, reducing the number of bunches the plant can carry that year. The result is a smaller crop. Hail also cuts yields, but by striking vines and grapes at any point in the season.":"春天葡萄樹正在長出新梢、葉子和花朵。這時的霜凍可能損害甚至凍死新生枝葉，減少植株當年能承載的果串數量。結果就是收成變少。冰雹也會降低產量，但它是在生長季的任何時候打傷葡萄樹和葡萄。","Which months does the growing season cover in the northern hemisphere?":"北半球的生長季涵蓋哪幾個月？","All year round, without a break":"全年無休","In the northern hemisphere the season runs April to October; in the southern, October to April.":"北半球的生長季是 4 月到 10 月；南半球是 10 月到 4 月。","The seasons are reversed between the hemispheres, and so is the growing season. October to April is the southern calendar, for example in Australia or Chile. The vine is dormant in winter, so it does not grow all year.":"南北半球的季節相反，生長季也是如此。10 月到 4 月是南半球的時間表，例如澳洲或智利。葡萄樹冬天休眠，所以不會全年生長。","A region has an average growing season temperature of 17.5°C. How is its climate classified?":"某產區生長季的平均溫度為 17.5°C。它的氣候屬於哪一類？","Too cold to ripen any grape variety":"太冷，任何葡萄品種都無法成熟","An average between 16.5°C and 18.5°C means a moderate climate.":"平均溫度介於 16.5°C 與 18.5°C 之間屬於溫和氣候。","Cool means 16.5°C or below, warm 18.5°C to 21°C. At 17.5°C the region sits in between. A moderate climate ripens many varieties, so the last option is wrong.":"涼爽是指 16.5°C 以下，溫暖是 18.5°C 至 21°C。17.5°C 的產區介於兩者之間。溫和氣候能讓許多品種成熟，所以最後一個選項是錯的。","Why is Chardonnay given as an example when discussing climate?":"討論氣候時，為什麼會以夏多內為例？","It grows well in different climates, but its flavours change with climate":"它在不同氣候中都長得好，但風味會隨氣候改變","It only ripens in warm climates":"它只在溫暖氣候中成熟","It tastes the same wherever it is grown":"無論種在哪裡，嚐起來都一樣","It can only be grown in cool climates, near rivers or the sea":"它只能種在涼爽氣候、靠近河流或海洋的地方","Chardonnay adapts to many climates, but develops different flavours depending on temperature.":"夏多內能適應多種氣候，但會依溫度發展出不同的風味。","Temperature decides both which varieties can grow and which flavours they develop. Grenache is the example of a variety that only ripens in warm climates. Chardonnay, by contrast, grows in cool, moderate and warm climates with different flavour profiles.":"溫度既決定哪些品種能種植，也決定它們發展出什麼風味。格那希是只在溫暖氣候中成熟的品種的例子。相反地，夏多內在涼爽、溫和和溫暖氣候中都能生長，風味特徵各不相同。","What effect do warm ocean currents have on the vineyards of northern Europe?":"溫暖洋流對北歐的葡萄園有什麼影響？","They warm them":"讓它們變暖","They cool them":"讓它們降溫","They bring fogs that encourage noble rot every vintage":"每個年份都帶來助長貴腐菌的霧氣","They have no effect":"沒有影響","In northern Europe, warm ocean currents have a warming influence on the climate.":"在北歐，溫暖洋流對氣候有增溫作用。","The sea moderates climate both ways. In South Africa's Cape, cold currents cool a warm climate; in northern Europe, warm currents help a cold one. The morning mists linked to noble rot come mainly from rivers in autumn.":"海洋對氣候的調節是雙向的。在南非的 Cape，寒冷洋流讓溫暖的氣候降溫；在北歐，溫暖洋流則幫助寒冷的氣候。與貴腐菌相關的晨霧主要來自秋天的河流。","How can mountains cool a warm vineyard lower down at night?":"山脈如何在夜間讓低處溫暖的葡萄園降溫？","Cold air flows down from the mountains to lower altitudes":"冷空氣從山上流向較低的海拔","They block warm ocean currents":"它們阻擋溫暖洋流","They shade the vineyard all night":"它們整晚為葡萄園遮蔭","They hold clouds over the vineyard and stop heat escaping":"它們把雲留在葡萄園上方，阻止熱量散失","At night cold mountain air moves downhill and cools vineyards where heat built up during the day.":"夜間，山上的冷空氣往下坡移動，讓白天累積熱量的葡萄園降溫。","Cool air, whether from the sea or mountains, moderates the climate. Shade means nothing at night, as the sun has already set. If anything, mountains shelter vineyards from cloud, rain and cold winds; they do not trap clouds over them.":"無論來自海洋還是山脈，涼爽的空氣都能調節氣候。遮蔭在夜間沒有意義，因為太陽已經下山了。山脈頂多是為葡萄園遮擋雲層、雨水和冷風，而不是把雲困在葡萄園上方。","A vineyard is sheltered by a mountain range. Which conditions is it most likely to enjoy?":"一座葡萄園受到山脈的屏障。它最可能享有哪些條件？","Sunny summers, dry autumns and a longer growing season":"陽光充足的夏天、乾燥的秋天和較長的生長季","More rain and more cloud":"更多雨水和雲層","Thick fog every summer morning":"每個夏日清晨都有濃霧","Constant cold winds that shorten ripening in autumn":"持續的冷風，縮短秋天的成熟期","Mountains act as a barrier to cloud, rain and cold winds, extending the season.":"山脈是阻擋雲、雨和冷風的屏障，能延長生長季。","Because they block cloud and rain, mountains bring sunny summers and dry autumns. Shelter from cold winds lets grapes ripen for longer, not shorter. Thick fogs are typical of some coastal areas, such as California and Chile.":"由於阻擋了雲和雨，山脈帶來陽光充足的夏天和乾燥的秋天。擋住冷風能讓葡萄成熟得更久，而不是更短。濃霧則是某些沿海地區的典型現象，例如加州和智利。","How can cloud slow down ripening in some warm Australian regions?":"在澳洲某些溫暖產區，雲層如何減緩成熟？","They block sunlight and slow photosynthesis":"它們遮擋陽光，減緩光合作用","They form at ground level and chill the roots":"它們在地面形成，讓根部受寒","They always bring hail, which reduces the crop":"它們總是帶來冰雹，減少收成","They raise humidity and encourage noble rot on the grapes every year":"它們提高濕度，每年都讓葡萄長出貴腐菌","Clouds form above ground and block the sun: less photosynthesis, slower ripening.":"雲在地面上方形成並遮住太陽：光合作用減少，成熟變慢。","This is an important moderating factor in some warm Australian regions. What forms at ground level is fog, not cloud. Noble rot needs morning mists followed by warm, dry afternoons instead.":"這是澳洲某些溫暖產區重要的調節因素。在地面形成的是霧，不是雲。貴腐菌需要的則是晨霧，加上溫暖乾燥的午後。","Which form of water vapour is essential for noble rot to develop?":"哪種形式的水氣對貴腐菌的發展不可或缺？","Autumn morning mists near rivers":"秋天清晨河流附近的薄霧","Low summer clouds that hide the sun for weeks":"連續數週遮住太陽的夏季低雲","Coastal Californian fog":"加州沿海的霧","Spring rain":"春雨","Mists rising from rivers on autumn mornings let the fungus develop.":"秋天早晨從河流升起的薄霧讓這種真菌得以發展。","Mist is a less dense form of fog. It must reach grapes that are already ripe, so in autumn, not spring. Coastal Californian fog mainly cools vineyards, while clouds block light and slow ripening.":"薄霧是比霧稀薄的形式。它必須接觸到已經成熟的葡萄，所以是在秋天，而不是春天。加州沿海的霧主要讓葡萄園降溫，而雲層則遮擋光線、減緩成熟。","Besides giving warmth in autumn, how else can a river help ripening far from the equator?":"在遠離赤道的地方，河流除了在秋天提供溫暖，還能以什麼方式幫助成熟？","It reflects sunlight onto the vines":"把陽光反射到葡萄樹上","It supplies nutrients to the leaves":"為葉片提供養分","It cools summers that are too hot":"讓過熱的夏天降溫","It prevents any mist from forming, so avoiding fungal disease":"阻止任何薄霧形成，從而避免真菌病害","The water's surface reflects light, which helps where sun and heat are scarce.":"水面反射光線，在陽光和熱量稀少的地方很有幫助。","Rivers warm up and cool down more slowly than land: in autumn they stay warmer, protect against frost and extend ripening. They do not feed the leaves, which take CO2 from the air. And river mists are exactly what encourages noble rot.":"河流升溫和降溫都比陸地慢：秋天時保持較溫暖，防止霜害並延長成熟期。它們不會餵養葉片，葉片是從空氣中吸收 CO2 的。而河流的薄霧正是助長貴腐菌的因素。","What is the soil's main role for the vine?":"土壤對葡萄樹的主要作用是什麼？","To supply water and nutrients":"提供水和養分","To supply carbon dioxide for photosynthesis":"為光合作用提供二氧化碳","To pollinate the flowers in spring":"在春天為花朵授粉","To protect the bunches from hail and birds during summer":"在夏天保護果串免受冰雹和鳥害","The soil must store enough water and nutrients to keep the vine healthy.":"土壤必須儲存足夠的水和養分，讓葡萄樹保持健康。","CO2 comes from the air through the leaves, not from the soil. Soil can also affect temperature: stones on the surface absorb heat and warm the vineyard. Against hail and birds, growers use nets, not soil.":"CO2 是透過葉片從空氣中取得的，不是來自土壤。土壤也可能影響溫度：地表的石頭吸收熱量，讓葡萄園變暖。對付冰雹和鳥類，種植者用的是網子，不是土壤。","A very hot, bright vintage: what risk do the grapes face?":"一個非常炎熱、陽光充足的年份：葡萄面臨什麼風險？","Untypical dried-fruit aromas and sunburn":"不典型的乾果香氣和日灼","Swollen grapes and diluted flavours":"葡萄膨脹，風味被稀釋","Strong herbaceous notes, as in grapes picked too early":"強烈的草本氣息，就像太早採收的葡萄","Excess heat and light can give untypical dried-fruit aromas and sunburn the grapes.":"過多的熱量和光照可能帶來不典型的乾果香氣，並讓葡萄日灼。","High acidity, little sugar and herbaceous notes are cool-vintage problems. Swollen grapes and diluted flavours come from heavy rain close to harvest. In extreme heat and drought, the vine may even shut down and fail to ripen its grapes.":"高酸、低糖和草本氣息是涼爽年份的問題。葡萄膨脹、風味稀釋則是採收前大雨造成的。在極端炎熱和乾旱下，葡萄樹甚至可能停止運作，無法讓葡萄成熟。","Why may grapes fail to ripen in a very hot summer with no rain?":"為什麼在非常炎熱又不下雨的夏天，葡萄可能無法成熟？","Short of water, the vine shuts down to protect itself":"缺水時，葡萄樹會停止運作以保護自己","The heat kills the yeasts on the skins and stops photosynthesis":"高溫殺死果皮上的酵母並中止光合作用","The grapes take up too much water from the roots":"葡萄從根部吸收了太多水","The leaves fall straight after flowering":"葉子在開花後立刻掉落","Heat increases the vine's need for water; without it, the vine shuts down and the grapes stop developing.":"高溫增加葡萄樹對水的需求；缺水時，葡萄樹停止運作，葡萄也停止發育。","High temperatures usually come with little rain, and in the worst cases the vine can die. Irrigation helps, but in these conditions there is often no water to use. Yeasts belong to fermentation in the winery, not ripening in the vineyard.":"高溫通常伴隨著少雨，最嚴重時葡萄樹可能死亡。灌溉有幫助，但在這種情況下往往無水可用。酵母屬於酒廠裡的發酵，不屬於葡萄園裡的成熟。","What causes drought?":"乾旱是什麼造成的？","Long periods of below-average rainfall, often made worse by heat":"長期降雨低於平均，常因高溫而更加嚴重","A single spring frost":"一次春霜","Too much irrigation":"過度灌溉","Coastal fog":"沿海的霧","Drought comes from prolonged low rainfall and worsens with above-average temperatures.":"乾旱來自長期的低降雨量，在溫度高於平均時會更嚴重。","In drought the vine cannot ripen its grapes and at worst it dies. Irrigation can help, but water is not always available. Frost damages new shoots and fog cools: neither causes drought.":"乾旱時葡萄樹無法讓葡萄成熟，最嚴重時會死亡。灌溉有幫助，但不一定有水可用。霜凍損害新梢，霧氣則帶來涼爽：兩者都不會造成乾旱。","What is the worst damage a heavy hailstorm can cause?":"一場猛烈的冰雹最嚴重會造成什麼損害？","Destroying the whole year's crop":"摧毀整年的收成","Slightly diluting the grapes' flavours":"輕微稀釋葡萄的風味","Starting noble rot on the ripe grapes":"讓成熟的葡萄開始長出貴腐菌","Delaying véraison by a few days with no effect on quality":"讓轉色期延後幾天，對品質沒有影響","Hail can badly damage vines and grapes, even wiping out the entire annual crop.":"冰雹可能嚴重損害葡萄樹和葡萄，甚至讓整年的收成化為烏有。","That is why, in some areas such as Argentina, growers stretch hail nets over the rows. Diluted flavours come from rain close to harvest. Noble rot needs morning mists and dry afternoons, not hail.":"所以在某些地區，例如阿根廷，種植者會在葡萄樹行上方架設防雹網。風味稀釋來自採收前的降雨。貴腐菌需要的是晨霧和乾燥的午後，而不是冰雹。","Why does a very wet season worry a grower even well before harvest?":"為什麼非常潮濕的季節，即使離採收還很久，也讓種植者擔心？","Moisture helps fungal diseases spread":"濕氣助長真菌病害蔓延","Rain stops photosynthesis for the whole summer":"下雨讓光合作用整個夏天都停止","Rain always increases the grapes' sugar":"下雨總是會提高葡萄的糖分","Rainwater stops the roots taking up any nutrients from the soil":"雨水讓根部無法從土壤吸收任何養分","High moisture helps fungi spread on leaves and grapes.":"高濕度助長真菌在葉片和葡萄上蔓延。","Fungal diseases reduce both the quality and the quantity of grapes. Close to harvest, rain also swells the grapes and dilutes flavours. Rain does not raise sugar; if anything, it dilutes it.":"真菌病害會同時降低葡萄的品質和產量。接近採收時，下雨還會讓葡萄膨脹、稀釋風味。下雨不會提高糖分；如果有影響，也是稀釋糖分。","Which statement about climate change and grape growing is correct?":"關於氣候變遷與葡萄種植，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","Average temperatures are rising and extreme events are more frequent":"平均溫度正在上升，極端事件也更加頻繁","Climate changes completely from one year to the next":"氣候每年都會徹底改變","It only affects air temperatures, not ocean temperatures":"它只影響氣溫，不影響海洋溫度","No producers or industry bodies are yet taking action to adapt":"還沒有任何生產者或產業組織採取調適行動","Records show a sustained rise in air and ocean temperatures, with more droughts and floods.":"紀錄顯示氣溫和海洋溫度持續上升，乾旱和洪水也變多了。","Climate does not change from year to year, but it can shift over decades; it is weather that varies each year. A growing number of producers and industry bodies are already acting to adapt and mitigate. The rise affects both air and oceans.":"氣候不會年年改變，但可能在數十年間轉變；每年變化的是天氣。越來越多生產者和產業組織已經採取行動，進行調適和減緩。溫度上升同時影響空氣和海洋。","When are vines usually pruned?":"葡萄樹通常在什麼時候修剪？","In winter, while the vine is dormant":"冬天，葡萄樹休眠時","In spring, during flowering":"春天，開花期間","In summer, at véraison":"夏天，轉色期時","In autumn, just before harvest":"秋天，就在採收前","Pruning is done in winter, when the vine is dormant, to keep its shape.":"修剪在冬天葡萄樹休眠時進行，以維持樹形。","Training and pruning ensure a healthy, commercially viable crop each year. Pruning is generally done in winter, when the vine is dormant and not growing, and it keeps each vine in its required shape. In spring and summer the plant is busy growing and then ripening its grapes.":"整枝和修剪能確保每年都有健康、具商業價值的收成。修剪一般在冬天進行，這時葡萄樹休眠、不生長，修剪能讓每株葡萄樹維持所需的樹形。春天和夏天，植株正忙著生長和讓葡萄成熟。","What are most vines trained on?":"大多數葡萄樹以什麼來整枝？","Trellises":"棚架","Trees":"樹木","Stone walls":"石牆","Hail nets":"防雹網","Most vines are trained on trellises of posts and wires.":"大多數葡萄樹以立柱和鐵絲組成的棚架來整枝。","Training gives the vine its shape and, together with pruning, helps produce a regular, healthy crop. In the vast majority of cases vines are supported by trellises of posts and wires. Nets serve other purposes, such as protecting against hail or keeping birds away.":"整枝賦予葡萄樹樹形，並與修剪一起幫助產出穩定、健康的收成。絕大多數情況下，葡萄樹由立柱和鐵絲組成的棚架支撐。網子則有其他用途，例如防冰雹或驅趕鳥類。","Why do most growers now use irrigation sparingly?":"為什麼現在大多數種植者都節制地使用灌溉？","Water is increasingly limited and expensive":"水越來越有限，也越來越貴","Irrigation is banned in all regions":"所有產區都禁止灌溉","Water makes sugar levels rise too much":"水會讓糖分上升太多","Irrigation causes spring frosts":"灌溉會引發春霜","Water is an increasingly limited and expensive resource.":"水是越來越有限、越來越昂貴的資源。","In regions with little rain, irrigation is usually allowed, with methods ranging from flooding the field to watering individual vines. However, water has become an increasingly limited and expensive resource, so it is used sparingly. In a severe drought, there is often no water available for irrigation anyway.":"在雨量少的產區，灌溉通常是允許的，方法從漫灌整片田地到為單株葡萄樹澆水都有。不過，水已經成為越來越有限、越來越昂貴的資源，所以要節制使用。而在嚴重乾旱時，往往根本無水可供灌溉。","Which product is used to kill fungi in the vineyard?":"葡萄園裡用哪種產品殺死真菌？","Fungicide":"殺菌劑","Insecticide":"殺蟲劑","Herbicide":"除草劑","Fertiliser":"肥料","Fungicides kill fungi; insecticides and herbicides target insects and weeds.":"殺菌劑殺死真菌；殺蟲劑和除草劑分別針對昆蟲和雜草。","Fungi and insects are hard to control, and one solution is chemical sprays. Fungicides act against fungi, insecticides against insects and herbicides against weeds. Because some of these products can cause longer-term problems, many growers try to use them as little as possible.":"真菌和昆蟲很難控制，其中一個解決方法是噴灑化學藥劑。殺菌劑對付真菌，殺蟲劑對付昆蟲，除草劑對付雜草。由於有些產品可能造成長期問題，許多種植者盡量少用。","What does it mean if a vineyard is certified organic?":"葡萄園獲得有機認證代表什麼？","Grapes are grown without most chemicals":"種植葡萄時不使用大部分化學藥劑","No sprays of any kind are ever used":"完全不使用任何噴灑藥劑","Grapes are always picked by hand":"葡萄一律人工採收","The maximum yield is set by law":"最高產量由法律規定","Organic growing avoids most chemicals, though some sprays are still permitted.":"有機種植避免使用大部分化學藥劑，但仍允許部分噴灑藥劑。","A certified organic vineyard does without most chemicals. It is not a total ban, though: some sprays are still allowed to keep the worst fungal diseases under control. Organic status says nothing about harvesting method or yields, which depend on other choices or rules.":"獲得有機認證的葡萄園不使用大部分化學藥劑。但這並非全面禁止：仍允許部分噴灑藥劑，以控制最嚴重的真菌病害。有機身分與採收方式或產量無關，那取決於其他選擇或法規。","What effect can an excessively high yield have on the grapes?":"產量過高會對葡萄造成什麼影響？","Diluted flavours and less sugar":"風味被稀釋，糖分較少","More concentrated flavours and more sugar":"風味更濃縮，糖分更多","Dried-fruit and raisin aromas":"乾果和葡萄乾的香氣","With yields too high, grapes can have diluted flavours and lower sugar.":"產量太高時，葡萄可能風味稀釋、糖分較低。","Yield measures how much fruit is produced per unit of area, and in some regions it is capped by law. If a vine carries too many bunches, the grapes can be lower in sugar with diluted flavours. On the other hand, with too few bunches the crop becomes too small to be commercially viable.":"產量衡量的是每單位面積生產多少果實，在某些產區有法定上限。如果一株葡萄樹掛了太多果串，葡萄可能糖分較低、風味稀釋。反過來說，果串太少，收成就太小，不具商業價值。","A producer wants a fresh white with crisp acidity. Which harvest choice helps most?":"一位生產者想釀出酸度爽脆的清爽白酒。哪種採收選擇最有幫助？","Picking earlier in the ripening process":"在成熟過程中較早採收","Picking very late":"非常晚才採收","Waiting for the grapes to shrivel":"等葡萄乾縮","Waiting for noble rot":"等貴腐菌出現","Grapes picked early have more acidity, less sugar and less-ripe flavours.":"較早採收的葡萄酸度較高、糖分較少、風味較不成熟。","Harvest timing changes the balance of the grapes. Picked early, they have higher acidity, less sugar and less-ripe flavours, ideal for a fresh style. Picking late, waiting for shrivelling or for noble rot instead brings more sugar and riper or more concentrated flavours, typical of richer or sweet wines.":"採收時機會改變葡萄的平衡。較早採收的葡萄酸度較高、糖分較少、風味較不成熟，非常適合清爽的風格。相反地，晚採、等待乾縮或等待貴腐菌，則帶來更多糖分和更成熟或更濃縮的風味，是較豐潤或甜型葡萄酒的典型特徵。","Which statement about hand and machine harvesting is correct?":"關於人工採收和機器採收，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","Machines cannot be used on steep slopes":"機器無法在陡坡上使用","Hand-picking always gives better wines":"人工採收總是釀出更好的酒","Machine picking always gives better wines":"機器採收總是釀出更好的酒","Machines are compulsory in organic vineyards":"有機葡萄園規定必須使用機器","Neither method is inherently better, but machines cannot work steep slopes.":"兩種方法本身沒有優劣之分，但機器無法在陡坡上作業。","Grapes can be picked by hand or by machine, and neither method is inherently better for wine quality. The choice usually depends on the style being made. There is one practical constraint, however: machine harvesters cannot work on steep slopes, where hand-picking is needed.":"葡萄可以用人工或機器採收，兩種方法本身對葡萄酒品質沒有優劣之分。選擇通常取決於要釀造的風格。不過有一個實際的限制：採收機無法在陡坡上作業，那裡需要人工採收。","How does the Botrytis fungus concentrate the sugar in a grape?":"貴腐菌如何濃縮葡萄中的糖分？","It makes tiny holes in the skin so water evaporates":"在果皮上造成微小的孔洞，讓水分蒸發","It turns the water in the grape into ice":"把葡萄裡的水變成冰","It adds sugar from its own growth":"藉由自身生長添加糖分","It blocks photosynthesis in the leaves":"阻斷葉片的光合作用","Botrytis pierces the skin, water evaporates, and sugars, acids and flavours concentrate.":"貴腐菌刺穿果皮，水分蒸發，糖、酸和風味隨之濃縮。","Noble rot is caused by the Botrytis fungus, which creates tiny holes in the skin. Water evaporates through these holes, concentrating acids, sugars and flavours. Turning water into ice is instead the mechanism behind the frozen grapes used for icewine. Grapes affected by noble rot nearly always go into sweet wines.":"貴腐是由貴腐菌（Botrytis）引起的，它會在果皮上造成微小的孔洞。水分從這些孔洞蒸發，使酸、糖和風味濃縮。把水變成冰則是用來釀造冰酒的冰凍葡萄的原理。受貴腐菌感染的葡萄幾乎都用來釀造甜酒。","Which weather conditions are ideal for beneficial noble rot?":"哪種天氣條件最適合有益的貴腐菌？","Damp misty mornings, then warm dry afternoons":"潮濕多霧的早晨，接著是溫暖乾燥的午後","Constant rain throughout autumn":"整個秋天持續下雨","Hot, dry days with no moisture at all":"炎熱乾燥、完全沒有濕氣的日子","Night frosts followed by cold days":"夜間霜凍，接著是寒冷的白天","Morning damp lets the fungus grow; warm, dry afternoons stop it destroying the grapes.":"早晨的濕氣讓真菌生長；溫暖乾燥的午後則阻止它毀掉葡萄。","Botrytis can easily destroy grapes, so it must act in a controlled way. First, the grapes must be ripe. Then damp, misty mornings, often from mists near rivers, allow the fungus to grow and spread, followed by warm, dry afternoons that limit its growth before it ruins the crop.":"貴腐菌很容易毀掉葡萄，所以它必須在受控的情況下作用。首先，葡萄必須已經成熟。接著，潮濕多霧的早晨（霧氣常來自河流附近）讓真菌生長蔓延，隨後溫暖乾燥的午後限制它的生長，以免毀掉收成。","Why are grapes for icewine pressed while still frozen?":"為什麼冰酒用的葡萄要在結冰狀態下壓榨？","The ice stays behind, leaving more concentrated juice":"冰留在壓榨機裡，留下更濃縮的果汁","The cold adds colour to the juice":"寒冷為果汁增添顏色","Freezing kills the noble rot on the grapes":"冰凍會殺死葡萄上的貴腐菌","Frozen grapes have more tannin":"結冰的葡萄單寧較多","Pressing frozen grapes leaves ice and skins behind, so the little juice is very concentrated.":"壓榨結冰的葡萄時，冰和果皮留在壓榨機裡，所以少量的果汁非常濃縮。","In frozen grapes much of the water has turned to ice. By pressing before they thaw, the ice crystals stay behind with the skins and only a small amount of unfrozen liquid runs off, very rich in acids, sugars and flavours. This is the basis of icewines: sweet, concentrated and with pure varietal character.":"在結冰的葡萄中，大部分的水已經變成冰。在解凍前壓榨，冰晶會和果皮一起留下，只有少量未結冰的液體流出，富含酸、糖和風味。這就是冰酒的基礎：甜美、濃縮，帶有純粹的品種特色。","What do extra-ripeness, noble rot and frozen grapes have in common?":"過熟、貴腐和冰凍葡萄有什麼共同點？","They concentrate sugar and are often used for sweet wines":"它們都會濃縮糖分，常用來釀造甜酒","They lower sugar and give dry, light wines":"它們會降低糖分，釀出不甜、輕盈的酒","They all need a warm climate with no fog":"它們都需要沒有霧氣的溫暖氣候","They mainly increase colour and tannin":"它們主要增加顏色和單寧","All three methods concentrate grape sugar, ideal for sweet wines.":"三種方法都會濃縮葡萄的糖分，非常適合釀造甜酒。","These are three different ways of getting very sweet grapes. With extra-ripeness, water slowly evaporates and the grapes shrivel; with noble rot, the fungus pierces the skin and water evaporates; with freezing, the water stays locked in ice during pressing. In every case sugars and acids are concentrated and the grapes suit sweet wines.":"這是取得非常甜的葡萄的三種不同方法。過熟時，水分緩慢蒸發，葡萄乾縮；貴腐時，真菌刺穿果皮，水分蒸發；冰凍時，水在壓榨過程中被鎖在冰裡。在每一種情況下，糖和酸都會濃縮，葡萄都適合釀造甜酒。","What is the main purpose of training and pruning vines?":"整枝和修剪葡萄樹的主要目的是什麼？","To get a healthy, commercially viable crop every year":"每年都獲得健康、具商業價值的收成","To make vineyards suitable only for hand harvesting":"讓葡萄園只適合人工採收","To push each vine's yield as high as possible, whatever the ripeness":"不管成熟度如何，盡可能提高每株葡萄樹的產量","To prevent winter dormancy":"防止冬季休眠","Training and pruning ensure a healthy, viable crop can be harvested successfully every year.":"整枝和修剪確保每年都能順利採收健康、具商業價值的收成。","Winter pruning keeps each vine in its required shape, and most vines are trained on trellises. An excessive yield dilutes flavour and sugar, so that is not the goal. Winter dormancy is natural and cannot be avoided.":"冬季修剪讓每株葡萄樹維持所需的樹形，而大多數葡萄樹以棚架整枝。過高的產量會稀釋風味和糖分，所以那不是目標。冬季休眠是自然現象，無法避免。","Which irrigation system can water each individual vine?":"哪一種灌溉系統可以為每一株葡萄樹單獨澆水？","Drip irrigation":"滴灌","Flooding the field":"漫灌整片田地","Digging a channel next to the vineyard to raise the river level":"在葡萄園旁挖渠道以抬高河水水位","A drip system delivers water directly to each vine.":"滴灌系統把水直接送到每一株葡萄樹。","Methods range from flooding the whole field to systems that measure water vine by vine. The latter are valuable because water is increasingly scarce and expensive. Fog cools a vineyard but is not an irrigation system.":"灌溉方法從漫灌整片田地，到逐株計量用水的系統都有。後者非常有價值，因為水越來越稀少、越來越昂貴。霧氣能讓葡萄園降溫，但它不是灌溉系統。","In which regions are growers normally allowed to irrigate?":"種植者通常在哪些產區被允許灌溉？","Where there is a lack of rainfall":"缺乏降雨的地方","Only in cool-climate regions":"只在涼爽氣候產區","Anywhere, without limit, even in very rainy areas":"任何地方都行，毫無限制，連多雨地區也一樣","Only in organic vineyards":"只在有機葡萄園","Irrigation is normally permitted in regions that lack rainfall.":"在缺乏降雨的產區，灌溉通常是允許的。","Irrigation makes up for a natural lack of water, typical of warm, dry areas rather than cool ones. Even where it is allowed, growers now use it sparingly because water is a limited resource. Organic rules are about chemicals, not water.":"灌溉是為了彌補天然的缺水，這是溫暖乾燥地區而非涼爽地區的典型問題。即使在允許灌溉的地方，種植者現在也節制使用，因為水是有限的資源。有機規範涉及的是化學藥劑，不是水。","A grower wants to control weeds with a chemical spray. What do they use?":"一位種植者想用化學噴劑控制雜草。他會用什麼？","A herbicide":"除草劑","A fungicide":"殺菌劑","An insecticide":"殺蟲劑","A fine mesh net stretched over the rows":"架在葡萄樹行上方的細網","Herbicides are used to control weeds.":"除草劑用來控制雜草。","Fungicides kill fungi and insecticides kill insects. Nets protect against birds, larger animals or hail, not weeds. Many growers try to limit these chemicals anyway, as they can cause longer-term problems.":"殺菌劑殺死真菌，殺蟲劑殺死昆蟲。網子防的是鳥類、較大的動物或冰雹，不是雜草。無論如何，許多種植者都盡量限制這些化學藥劑，因為它們可能造成長期問題。","How are grapes most easily protected from birds and larger animals?":"保護葡萄免受鳥類和較大動物侵害，最簡單的方法是什麼？","With nets and fences":"用網子和圍欄","With fungicides sprayed on the leaves":"在葉片上噴灑殺菌劑","With shorter pruning in summer":"夏天修剪得更短","By harvesting just after fruit set, before the grapes turn sweet":"在著果後、葡萄變甜之前就採收","Birds and animals are kept away with physical barriers such as nets and fences.":"用網子和圍欄等實體屏障讓鳥類和動物遠離。","Large pests are fairly easy to keep out; fungi and insects are much harder to control. Fungicides act on fungi, not birds. Harvesting right after fruit set would give hard, green, inedible grapes.":"大型害物相對容易阻擋；真菌和昆蟲則難控制得多。殺菌劑作用於真菌，不是鳥類。著果後立刻採收，得到的會是又硬又綠、無法食用的葡萄。","In some areas, such as Argentina, nets are stretched over the vines. What are they mainly for?":"在某些地區，例如阿根廷，葡萄樹上方會架設網子。它們主要用來做什麼？","Against hail":"防冰雹","Against spring frost":"防春霜","To hold fog over the vineyard":"把霧氣留在葡萄園上方","To stop the roots taking up too much water after summer storms":"防止根部在夏季暴雨後吸收太多水","Hail nets shield vines and bunches from hailstones.":"防雹網保護葡萄樹和果串免受冰雹打擊。","A violent hailstorm can destroy a whole crop, and a net is an effective physical barrier. A net does little against frost, as the cold gets through anyway. Nets have no effect on fog or roots.":"一場猛烈的冰雹可能摧毀整年的收成，而網子是有效的實體屏障。網子對霜凍幫助不大，因為寒冷照樣會穿透。網子對霧氣或根部都沒有影響。","Why do many growers try to limit their use of chemical sprays?":"為什麼許多種植者盡量限制使用化學噴劑？","They can cause longer-term problems in vineyards":"它們可能在葡萄園造成長期問題","They are banned in every wine region except outside the EU":"除了歐盟以外，所有葡萄酒產區都禁止使用","They make wine sweeter":"它們讓葡萄酒更甜","They have no effect on fungi or insects":"它們對真菌或昆蟲沒有作用","Some of these chemicals can cause longer-term problems in vineyards.":"其中一些化學藥劑可能在葡萄園造成長期問題。","Fungicides, insecticides and herbicides do work, which is why they are used. They are not banned everywhere; organic growing uses very few, but some sprays against the worst fungal diseases are still allowed. A wine's sweetness has nothing to do with them.":"殺菌劑、殺蟲劑和除草劑確實有效，所以才會被使用。它們並非到處都被禁止；有機種植用得很少，但仍允許部分對付最嚴重真菌病害的噴劑。葡萄酒的甜度與它們無關。","Which statement about a certified organic vineyard is correct?":"關於獲得有機認證的葡萄園，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","Some sprays against the worst fungal diseases are still allowed":"仍允許部分對付最嚴重真菌病害的噴劑","No sprays of any kind are allowed":"不允許任何噴劑","Harvesting must be done by machine":"必須用機器採收","Irrigation is banned and vines must live on rainwater alone":"禁止灌溉，葡萄樹只能靠雨水生存","Organic growing avoids most chemicals, but some anti-fungal sprays remain permitted.":"有機種植避免使用大部分化學藥劑，但仍允許部分抗真菌噴劑。","'Organic' on a label means grapes grown without most chemicals, not with no treatment at all. The rules do not impose a harvesting method. Irrigation depends on lack of rainfall, not on organic status.":"酒標上的「有機」代表種植葡萄時不使用大部分化學藥劑，而不是完全不做任何處理。法規並未規定採收方式。灌溉與否取決於是否缺乏降雨，與有機身分無關。","Where do the fungi that attack vines grow, and what harm do they do?":"侵襲葡萄樹的真菌長在哪裡？會造成什麼危害？","On grapes and leaves; they reduce grape quality and quantity":"長在葡萄和葉片上；會降低葡萄的品質和產量","Only on the roots; they lower the wine's alcohol":"只長在根部；會降低葡萄酒的酒精濃度","Only on the trunk; they never touch the grapes":"只長在主幹上；從不接觸葡萄","In winery barrels; they add vanilla and coconut notes to the wine":"長在酒廠的橡木桶裡；為酒增添香草和椰子氣息","Fungi grow on grapes and leaves and can greatly reduce crop quality and quantity.":"真菌長在葡萄和葉片上，可能大幅降低收成的品質和產量。","Vines are vulnerable to many fungal diseases, sometimes with very serious damage. That is why fungicides are used, partly even in organic vineyards. Vanilla and coconut come from new oak, not a fungus.":"葡萄樹容易感染許多真菌病害，有時損害非常嚴重。這就是為什麼要使用殺菌劑，甚至有機葡萄園也部分使用。香草和椰子來自新橡木桶，不是真菌。","What is the problem if a vine produces too few grapes?":"如果一株葡萄樹結的葡萄太少，會有什麼問題？","The crop is too small to be commercially viable":"收成太小，不具商業價值","The flavours become diluted":"風味變得稀釋","The grapes always have less sugar":"葡萄的糖分總是比較少","The wine automatically becomes a late harvest wine":"酒會自動變成晚收酒","With too low a yield, there is not enough fruit for the vineyard to pay its way.":"產量太低時，果實不夠多，葡萄園無法回本。","Growers look for a balance: too many grapes give diluted flavours and less sugar, too few do not pay. Dilution and low sugar are therefore the risks of excessive yields, not low ones. 'Late harvest' depends on picking date, not yield.":"種植者追求的是平衡：葡萄太多會稀釋風味、降低糖分，太少則不划算。所以稀釋和低糖是產量過高的風險，而不是產量過低。「晚收」取決於採收日期，與產量無關。","Which statement about yield is correct?":"關於產量，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","In some regions the maximum yield is set by law":"在某些產區，最高產量由法律規定","Yield measures the finished wine's alcohol":"產量衡量的是成品酒的酒精濃度","The higher the yield, the more concentrated the flavours":"產量越高，風味越濃縮","Yield depends only on climate and the grower cannot influence it in any way":"產量只取決於氣候，種植者完全無法影響","Yield is fruit produced per unit of area, and in some regions the law sets a maximum.":"產量是每單位面積生產的果實量，在某些產區法律訂有上限。","Excessive yields dilute flavours and lower sugar rather than concentrating them. Yield measures the amount of fruit, not alcohol. Pruning and vineyard management exist precisely to regulate the crop.":"過高的產量會稀釋風味、降低糖分，而不是讓它們濃縮。產量衡量的是果實的數量，不是酒精。修剪和葡萄園管理正是為了調節收成而存在。","A producer harvests later than usual. What kind of grapes should they expect?":"一位生產者比平常晚採收。他應該預期得到什麼樣的葡萄？","More sugar, less acidity and riper flavours":"糖分較多、酸度較低、風味較成熟","Less sugar, more acidity and greener flavours":"糖分較少、酸度較高、風味較青澀","The same sugar and acidity, but paler skins":"糖分和酸度相同，但果皮顏色較淺","More acidity and more unripe tannins":"酸度較高，未成熟的單寧較多","Picking later means higher sugar, lower acidity and riper flavours.":"較晚採收代表糖分較高、酸度較低、風味較成熟。","Harvest timing is a key style decision. More acidity, less sugar and less ripe flavours come from picking early. If grapes stay on the vine even longer, they shrivel and take on raisin notes.":"採收時機是關鍵的風格決定。酸度較高、糖分較少、風味較不成熟來自較早採收。如果葡萄在樹上留得更久，就會乾縮並帶有葡萄乾的氣息。","Between hand and machine harvesting, which gives better-quality wine?":"人工採收和機器採收，哪一種能釀出品質更好的酒？","Neither is fundamentally better":"兩者本質上沒有優劣之分","Always hand harvesting":"永遠是人工採收","Always machine harvesting":"永遠是機器採收","Machine on steep slopes, hand only on flat land":"陡坡用機器，平地才用人工","Neither method is fundamentally better: the choice mainly depends on the wine style.":"兩種方法本質上沒有優劣之分：選擇主要取決於葡萄酒的風格。","The practical limit is that machines cannot work on steep slopes, where hand picking is needed; the last option gets this backwards. Always linking hand picking with quality is a cliché, not a rule.":"實際的限制是機器無法在陡坡上作業，那裡需要人工採收；最後一個選項正好說反了。總是把人工採收和品質畫上等號只是刻板印象，不是規則。","Which condition is essential for Botrytis to be 'noble' rather than destructive?":"貴腐菌要成為「貴腐」而非破壞性的，哪個條件不可或缺？","It must grow on grapes that are already ripe":"它必須長在已經成熟的葡萄上","It must attack grapes just after fruit set":"它必須在著果後立刻侵襲葡萄","It must rain heavily every afternoon":"每天下午都必須下大雨","The grapes must freeze on the vine before the fungus appears":"葡萄必須在真菌出現之前就在樹上結冰","The fungus is only beneficial on ripe grapes, with the right weather.":"這種真菌只有在成熟的葡萄上、配合合適的天氣，才是有益的。","Botrytis can easily destroy grapes. It needs ripe grapes, then damp, misty mornings to grow and warm, dry afternoons to hold it back. Afternoon rain would let it run out of control; freezing relates to icewine instead.":"貴腐菌很容易毀掉葡萄。它需要成熟的葡萄，接著需要潮濕多霧的早晨讓它生長，以及溫暖乾燥的午後抑制它。午後下雨會讓它失控；結冰則與冰酒有關。","In the development of noble rot, what is the role of warm, dry afternoons?":"在貴腐菌的發展過程中，溫暖乾燥的午後扮演什麼角色？","To limit the fungus so it does not destroy the grapes":"抑制真菌，以免它毀掉葡萄","To start the fungus growing on the grapes":"讓真菌開始在葡萄上生長","To freeze the water in the grapes":"讓葡萄裡的水結冰","To add water to the grapes to dilute acidity before harvest":"在採收前為葡萄補水以稀釋酸度","Warm, dry afternoons slow the fungus and stop it ruining the grapes.":"溫暖乾燥的午後減緩真菌生長，阻止它毀掉葡萄。","Damp, misty mornings are what allow the fungus to grow and spread. Alternating the two creates noble rot, which evaporates water and concentrates sugars, acids and flavours. Freezing grapes is the icewine technique.":"讓真菌生長蔓延的是潮濕多霧的早晨。兩者交替就形成貴腐，使水分蒸發，糖、酸和風味濃縮。冰凍葡萄則是冰酒的技術。","What style of wine is usually made from grapes frozen on the vine (icewine)?":"用在樹上結冰的葡萄（冰酒）通常釀成什麼風格的酒？","Sweet, concentrated and with pure varietal character":"甜美、濃縮，帶有純粹的品種特色","Dry and light, with flavours diluted by the ice water":"不甜、輕盈，風味被冰水稀釋","A tannic red for long ageing":"適合長期陳年的高單寧紅酒","Sweet, with strong noble-rot and raisin notes":"甜，帶有強烈的貴腐和葡萄乾氣息","Pressing healthy frozen grapes gives a little juice rich in sugar, acid and pure flavours: sweet, concentrated wines.":"壓榨健康的結冰葡萄，能得到少量富含糖、酸和純粹風味的果汁：釀出甜美濃縮的酒。","For icewine, healthy grapes stay on the vine through autumn into winter, are picked frozen and pressed before they thaw. Ice and skins stay in the press, so there is no dilution. Noble-rot and raisin notes belong to other concentration methods.":"釀造冰酒時，健康的葡萄從秋天一直留在樹上到冬天，在結冰狀態下採收，並在解凍前壓榨。冰和果皮留在壓榨機裡，所以不會被稀釋。貴腐和葡萄乾氣息屬於其他的濃縮方法。","A legally defined vineyard area":"法律界定的葡萄園區域","A grape variety permitted in a region":"某產區允許使用的葡萄品種","A brand registered by a producer":"生產者註冊的品牌","A quality ranking of vintages":"年份的品質排名","A GI is a legally defined vineyard area, large or small.":"GI 是法律界定的葡萄園區域，可大可小。","A GI legally defines a vineyard area. It can be very large, up to a whole region or country, or very small, such as a single vineyard. GIs appear on labels worldwide because the place where grapes grow can influence wine style. Not every wine comes from a GI, but some statement of origin must always be given.":"GI（地理標示）在法律上界定一個葡萄園區域。它可以非常大，大到整個產區或國家，也可以非常小，例如單一葡萄園。世界各地的酒標上都有 GI，因為葡萄生長的地方會影響葡萄酒的風格。並非每一款酒都來自某個 GI，但一定要標示某種產地說明。","Why is an EU GI a more reliable guide to style than a GI outside the EU?":"為什麼歐盟的 GI 比歐盟以外的 GI 更能可靠地反映風格？","It has rules on permitted grapes and winemaking":"它對允許的品種和釀造方式有規定","It always covers larger areas":"它涵蓋的區域總是比較大","It always names the grape on the label":"它總是在酒標上標示品種","It bans the use of irrigation":"它禁止灌溉","In the EU each GI sets which grapes may be grown and how the wine is made.":"在歐盟，每個 GI 都規定可以種植哪些品種，以及酒要如何釀造。","Outside the EU, a GI mainly shows where the grapes were grown: growers plant what they like and rules are minimal, so styles vary widely. In the EU, each GI adds rules on permitted varieties and winemaking methods. That is why an EU GI tells you much more about the expected style, even without the grape name.":"在歐盟以外，GI 主要表示葡萄種植的地點：種植者想種什麼就種什麼，規定極少，所以風格差異很大。在歐盟，每個 GI 還加上允許品種和釀造方式的規定。這就是為什麼即使沒有標示品種，歐盟的 GI 也能告訴你更多關於預期風格的資訊。","Which description best fits a PDO compared with a PGI?":"與 PGI 相比，哪一項描述最符合 PDO？","Smaller area and stricter rules":"區域較小，規定較嚴格","Wider area and more flexible rules":"區域較廣，規定較彈性","No rules on which grapes to use":"對使用的品種沒有規定","Only inexpensive high-volume wines":"只有平價的大量生產酒款","PDOs usually cover small areas with tight rules; PGIs are wider and more flexible.":"PDO 通常涵蓋小區域、規定嚴格；PGI 則區域較廣、較有彈性。","PDOs generally cover relatively small areas with tight regulations and include many of Europe's most prestigious wines. PGIs cover much wider areas with less strict rules, giving more freedom over grapes and techniques. PGI wines range from inexpensive high-volume wines to outstanding, premium-priced ones, so they are not only simple wines.":"PDO（受保護原產地名稱）一般涵蓋相對較小的區域，規定嚴格，包括歐洲許多最負盛名的葡萄酒。PGI（受保護地理標示）涵蓋廣得多的區域，規定較寬鬆，在品種和技術上給予更多自由。PGI 葡萄酒從平價的大量生產酒款到價格高昂的傑出酒款都有，所以不只是簡單的酒。","Which French term indicates a PGI?":"哪一個法文術語代表 PGI？","In France PGI is Indication géographique protégée; AOC and AOP indicate PDO.":"在法國，PGI 是 Indication géographique protégée；AOC 和 AOP 代表 PDO。","France uses two terms for PDO: Appellation d'origine protégée (AOP) and the traditional Appellation d'origine contrôlée (AOC). For PGI it uses Indication géographique protégée (IGP). Vieilles vignes, on the other hand, means old vines and is not even a legally defined term.":"法國的 PDO 有兩個術語：Appellation d'origine protégée（AOP）和傳統的 Appellation d'origine contrôlée（AOC）。PGI 則使用 Indication géographique protégée（IGP）。另一方面，Vieilles vignes 的意思是老藤，甚至不是法律定義的術語。","Which Italian term corresponds to PGI?":"哪一個義大利文術語對應 PGI？","In Italy PGI is Indicazione Geografica Tipica (IGT); DOC and DOCG are PDO.":"在義大利，PGI 是 Indicazione Geografica Tipica（IGT）；DOC 和 DOCG 是 PDO。","Italy has two traditional terms for PDO: Denominazione di Origine Controllata (DOC) and Denominazione di Origine Controllata e Garantita (DOCG). For PGI it uses Indicazione Geografica Tipica (IGT). DOCa is a Spanish term, Denominación de Origen Calificada, which belongs to the PDO category.":"義大利的 PDO 有兩個傳統術語：Denominazione di Origine Controllata（DOC）和 Denominazione di Origine Controllata e Garantita（DOCG）。PGI 則使用 Indicazione Geografica Tipica（IGT）。DOCa 是西班牙術語 Denominación de Origen Calificada，屬於 PDO 類別。","Which Spanish term indicates a PGI?":"哪一個西班牙文術語代表 PGI？","In Spain PGI is Vino de la Tierra; DO and DOCa are PDO.":"在西班牙，PGI 是 Vino de la Tierra；DO 和 DOCa 是 PDO。","In Spain, PDO is expressed by Denominación de Origen (DO) and Denominación de Origen Calificada (DOCa), while PGI is called Vino de la Tierra. Landwein is also a PGI term, but it is German, not Spanish, so it is the trap to avoid here.":"在西班牙，PDO 以 Denominación de Origen（DO）和 Denominación de Origen Calificada（DOCa）表示，而 PGI 稱為 Vino de la Tierra。Landwein 也是 PGI 術語，但它是德文，不是西班牙文，所以這是要避開的陷阱。","In Germany, which term corresponds to PGI?":"在德國，哪一個術語對應 PGI？","Germany's PGI term is Landwein; Qualitätswein and Prädikatswein are PDO.":"德國的 PGI 術語是 Landwein；Qualitätswein 和 Prädikatswein 是 PDO。","In Germany there are two traditional terms for PDO, Qualitätswein and Prädikatswein, while PGI corresponds to Landwein. Eiswein is not an origin category at all: it is a grape-growing term meaning the grapes were left to freeze on the vine before harvest.":"德國的 PDO 有兩個傳統術語：Qualitätswein 和 Prädikatswein，而 PGI 對應 Landwein。Eiswein 根本不是產地類別：它是葡萄種植術語，意思是葡萄在採收前留在樹上結冰。","A label reads Appellation Chablis Contrôlée but names no grape. Which grape is the wine made from?":"一張酒標上寫著 Appellation Chablis Contrôlée，但沒有標示品種。這款酒是用哪個品種釀的？","Chablis rules require Chardonnay, even though it is not shown on the label.":"Chablis 的法規規定使用夏多內，即使酒標上沒有標示。","Chablis is a French GI, and Appellation Contrôlée is the traditional French term for PDO. The rules of this appellation require the wines to be made from Chardonnay. For European PDO wines the grape does not have to appear on the label, so knowing the rules of the area tells you what is in the bottle.":"Chablis 是法國的 GI，而 Appellation Contrôlée 是法國 PDO 的傳統術語。這個法定產區的法規要求以夏多內釀造。歐洲的 PDO 葡萄酒不必在酒標上標示品種，所以了解產區法規就能知道瓶中是什麼。","Why are wines from old vines often highly prized?":"為什麼老藤釀的酒常常備受珍視？","Fewer grapes, with more concentrated, complex aromas":"葡萄較少，香氣更濃縮、更複雜","Higher yields with fresher aromas":"產量較高，香氣更清新","The term legally guarantees a minimum age":"這個術語在法律上保證最低樹齡","They are always sweet wines from shrivelled grapes":"它們總是用乾縮葡萄釀的甜酒","Old vines produce smaller crops, often with more concentrated, complex fruit.":"老藤的收成較小，果實常常更濃縮、更複雜。","As vines age, they tend to produce fewer bunches. A smaller crop can give grapes with more concentrated and complex aromas, and so higher-quality wines. That is why such wines are often labelled Old Vine or vieilles vignes. However, the term is not legally defined, so it guarantees no minimum age and its use can be disputed.":"隨著樹齡增長，葡萄樹結的果串往往變少。較小的收成可能帶來香氣更濃縮、更複雜的葡萄，因而釀出品質更高的酒。這就是為什麼這類酒常標示 Old Vine 或 vieilles vignes。不過，這個術語沒有法律定義，所以不保證任何最低樹齡，其使用也可能引起爭議。","An Australian and a Californian wine are both labelled 2022. Which statement is correct?":"一款澳洲酒和一款加州酒都標示 2022。下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","The Australian wine is about six months older":"澳洲酒大約老六個月","The Californian wine is about six months older":"加州酒大約老六個月","They are exactly the same age":"兩者年齡完全相同","The Australian wine is about a year older":"澳洲酒大約老一年","The southern hemisphere harvest comes about six months before the northern one.":"南半球的採收比北半球早大約六個月。","The vintage is the year of harvest. In the southern hemisphere the growing season runs from October to April, so grapes are picked early in the year; in the northern hemisphere it runs from April to October, with harvest towards the end of the year. An Australian 2022 is therefore about half a year older than a Californian 2022.":"年份是採收的年份。南半球的生長季從 10 月到 4 月，所以葡萄在年初採收；北半球則從 4 月到 10 月，在接近年底時採收。因此，2022 年的澳洲酒比 2022 年的加州酒大約老半年。","What does the term Late Harvest on a label indicate?":"酒標上的 Late Harvest 代表什麼？","Grapes picked well after the normal time":"葡萄在正常時間之後很久才採收","Grapes affected by noble rot":"葡萄受到貴腐菌感染","Grapes frozen on the vine":"葡萄在樹上結冰","Grapes from vines at least 60 years old":"葡萄來自至少 60 年樹齡的葡萄樹","Late Harvest means grapes left on the vine and picked much later than usual.":"Late Harvest 是指葡萄留在樹上，比平常晚很多才採收。","Late Harvest wines are made from grapes left on the vine beyond the normal picking time. The grapes have riper flavours and more sugar, and the wines are fuller-bodied and more concentrated than those from grapes picked at the usual time. Noble rot and frozen grapes have their own terms: Botrytis/Noble Rot and icewine/Eiswein.":"Late Harvest（晚收）葡萄酒是用留在樹上超過正常採收時間的葡萄釀造的。這些葡萄風味更成熟、糖分更多，釀出的酒比正常時間採收的葡萄酒體更飽滿、更濃縮。貴腐和冰凍葡萄則有各自的術語：Botrytis/Noble Rot 以及 icewine/Eiswein。","Which statement about a wine labelled Late Harvest is correct?":"關於標示 Late Harvest 的酒，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","It can be dry, off-dry, medium or sweet":"它可以是不甜、微甜、半甜或甜","It is always a sweet wine":"它一定是甜酒","It is always lighter than a normal wine":"它一定比一般的酒輕盈","It is always made from frozen grapes":"它一定是用冰凍葡萄釀的","Late Harvest wines are fuller and more concentrated, but their sweetness varies.":"Late Harvest 葡萄酒更飽滿、更濃縮，但甜度不一。","Late-picked grapes have more sugar and riper flavours, giving fuller-bodied, more concentrated wines. That does not mean the wine must be sweet: a Late Harvest wine can be dry, off-dry, medium or sweet. By contrast, grapes with noble rot nearly always go into sweet wines, and icewine uses frozen grapes, not just late-picked ones.":"晚採的葡萄糖分更多、風味更成熟，釀出酒體更飽滿、更濃縮的酒。但這不代表酒一定是甜的：Late Harvest 葡萄酒可以是不甜、微甜、半甜或甜。相對地，受貴腐菌感染的葡萄幾乎都用來釀甜酒，而冰酒用的是冰凍的葡萄，不只是晚採的葡萄。","Which statement about the size of a geographical indication (GI) is correct?":"關於地理標示（GI）的大小，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","It can range from a single vineyard to a whole country":"它可以從單一葡萄園到整個國家","It must always match one village":"它必須總是對應一個村莊","It can never exceed 100 hectares":"它絕不能超過 100 公頃","It always covers a whole administrative region, never a smaller area":"它總是涵蓋整個行政區，絕不會是較小的區域","A GI is a legally defined vineyard area, as large as a country or as small as one vineyard.":"GI 是法律界定的葡萄園區域，可以大如一個國家，也可以小如一座葡萄園。","GIs appear on labels because where grapes are grown influences the wine's style. There is no fixed size and no required link to administrative borders. For example, 'South Eastern Australia' is a very large GI, while others are tiny.":"酒標上出現 GI，是因為葡萄種植的地點會影響酒的風格。GI 沒有固定大小，也不必與行政邊界對應。例如「South Eastern Australia」是非常大的 GI，而其他有些則非常小。","A wine does not come from any GI. Which statement of origin must still appear on the label, where applicable?":"一款酒不來自任何 GI。酒標上仍必須標示哪一種產地說明（如適用）？","The country of origin":"原產國","The vineyard name":"葡萄園名稱","The age of the vines":"葡萄樹的樹齡","The exact harvest date and the names of the pickers":"確切的採收日期和採收者的姓名","Not every wine has a GI, but some statement of origin is required, such as the country.":"並非每一款酒都有 GI，但必須標示某種產地說明，例如國家。","A vineyard name is used only when the wine truly comes from it, and is often a GI itself. Vine age ('old vines') is optional and not legally defined. Exact dates and pickers' names do not appear on labels.":"葡萄園名稱只有在酒確實來自該葡萄園時才會使用，而且它本身常常就是一個 GI。樹齡（「老藤」）是選擇性的，沒有法律定義。確切日期和採收者姓名不會出現在酒標上。","A customer is looking at a wine from a non-EU GI and wants to predict its style. What is most useful to check on the label?":"一位顧客在看一款來自歐盟以外 GI 的酒，想預測它的風格。酒標上最值得查看的是什麼？","The grape variety":"葡萄品種","The GI name alone":"只看 GI 名稱","The colour of the capsule":"瓶封的顏色","The bottle size, which varies with the style of wine":"酒瓶容量，它會隨葡萄酒風格而不同","Outside the EU a GI only shows where the grapes grew, so the grape variety is the best clue.":"在歐盟以外，GI 只表示葡萄生長的地點，所以葡萄品種是最好的線索。","Outside the EU growers can plant whatever varieties they like, with few restrictions, so one place name can cover very different styles. That is why these wines are often varietally labelled. Capsule colour and bottle size tell you nothing reliable about style.":"在歐盟以外，種植者可以種任何想種的品種，限制很少，所以同一個地名可能涵蓋非常不同的風格。這就是為什麼這些酒常以品種標示。瓶封顏色和酒瓶容量都無法可靠地反映風格。","Which pair of Italian terms both indicate a PDO?":"下列哪一組義大利術語都代表 PDO？","IGT and DOC":"IGT 和 DOC","IGT and DOCG":"IGT 和 DOCG","IGT and table wine showing a region":"IGT 和標示產區的餐酒","In Italy DOC and DOCG are the traditional terms for PDO; IGT corresponds to PGI.":"在義大利，DOC 和 DOCG 是 PDO 的傳統術語；IGT 對應 PGI。","Each EU country uses its own traditional terms for the two categories. Any pair containing IGT mixes a PDO with a PGI. PDOs usually cover smaller areas with stricter rules.":"每個歐盟國家都用自己的傳統術語表示這兩個類別。任何包含 IGT 的組合都把 PDO 和 PGI 混在一起了。PDO 通常涵蓋較小的區域，規定較嚴格。","A Spanish label shows 'DOCa'. What does this tell you?":"一張西班牙酒標上寫著「DOCa」。這告訴你什麼？","That the wine is a PDO":"這款酒是 PDO","That the wine is a PGI":"這款酒是 PGI","That the wine is made from frozen grapes":"這款酒是用冰凍葡萄釀的","That the wine has no GI and comes from several countries":"這款酒沒有 GI，來自多個國家","In Spain, DO and DOCa are traditional terms for PDO.":"在西班牙，DO 和 DOCa 是 PDO 的傳統術語。","Spain's PGI term is Vino de la Tierra. DOCa (Denominación de Origen Calificada) belongs to the tier with smaller areas and tighter rules. It has nothing to do with frozen grapes, which is how icewine is made.":"西班牙的 PGI 術語是 Vino de la Tierra。DOCa（Denominación de Origen Calificada）屬於區域較小、規定較嚴格的等級。它與冰凍葡萄無關，冰凍葡萄是冰酒的釀法。","A German label says 'Prädikatswein'. Which EU category does the wine belong to?":"一張德國酒標上寫著「Prädikatswein」。這款酒屬於哪個歐盟類別？","Wine with no geographical indication":"沒有地理標示的葡萄酒","A category reserved for certified organic wines":"專屬於有機認證葡萄酒的類別","In Germany, Qualitätswein and Prädikatswein correspond to PDO; Landwein to PGI.":"在德國，Qualitätswein 和 Prädikatswein 對應 PDO；Landwein 對應 PGI。","Landwein is Germany's PGI term, with looser rules. Prädikatswein, like Qualitätswein, belongs to the higher tier. Organic is a separate certification, unrelated to the origin category.":"Landwein 是德國的 PGI 術語，規定較寬鬆。Prädikatswein 和 Qualitätswein 一樣屬於較高的等級。有機是另一種認證，與產地類別無關。","In France, what is the difference between AOC and AOP on a label?":"在法國，酒標上的 AOC 和 AOP 有什麼不同？","None: both are terms for the same PDO category":"沒有不同：兩者都是同一個 PDO 類別的術語","AOC is a PDO, AOP is a PGI":"AOC 是 PDO，AOP 是 PGI","AOP is used only for sweet wines":"AOP 只用於甜酒","AOC means organic, while AOP means a wine from old vines":"AOC 代表有機，而 AOP 代表老藤釀的酒","Appellation d'origine contrôlée and appellation d'origine protégée both indicate PDO.":"Appellation d'origine contrôlée 和 appellation d'origine protégée 都代表 PDO。","France's PGI term is Indication géographique protégée (IGP). AOC is the traditional term and is still widely seen, as in 'Appellation Chablis Contrôlée'. Neither term has anything to do with organic status, sweetness or vine age.":"法國的 PGI 術語是 Indication géographique protégée（IGP）。AOC 是傳統術語，至今仍很常見，例如「Appellation Chablis Contrôlée」。這兩個術語都與有機身分、甜度或樹齡無關。","Which of these terms does NOT indicate a PDO?":"下列哪一個術語不代表 PDO？","IGT is Italy's PGI term; the other three all indicate a PDO.":"IGT 是義大利的 PGI 術語；其他三個都代表 PDO。","DOCa (Spain), Qualitätswein (Germany) and AOC (France) all belong to the PDO tier. PGIs cover wider areas, with more freedom over grapes and techniques. That is why one producer's IGT wines can differ widely.":"DOCa（西班牙）、Qualitätswein（德國）和 AOC（法國）都屬於 PDO 等級。PGI 涵蓋較廣的區域，在品種和技術上有更多自由。這就是為什麼同一家生產者的 IGT 葡萄酒可能差異很大。","Which of these terms does NOT indicate a PGI?":"下列哪一個術語不代表 PGI？","DOC is an Italian PDO term; Landwein, Vino de la Tierra and IGP all indicate PGI.":"DOC 是義大利的 PDO 術語；Landwein、Vino de la Tierra 和 IGP 都代表 PGI。","Watch out for similar acronyms: Italy's DOC is a PDO, as is Spain's DO. The PGI terms are Landwein in Germany, Vino de la Tierra in Spain, IGP in France and IGT in Italy. Learning the table country by country avoids mix-ups.":"小心相似的縮寫：義大利的 DOC 是 PDO，西班牙的 DO 也是。PGI 術語在德國是 Landwein，在西班牙是 Vino de la Tierra，在法國是 IGP，在義大利是 IGT。逐國記住這張表就不會混淆。","Which statement about PGI wines is correct?":"關於 PGI 葡萄酒，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","They range from cheap, high-volume wines to outstanding low-volume wines":"從便宜的大量生產酒款，到產量稀少的傑出酒款都有","They are always lower in quality than any PDO":"品質一定比任何 PDO 都低","They must be made from one grape only":"必須只用單一品種釀造","They have stricter rules than PDOs on grapes and winemaking":"在品種和釀造方面的規定比 PDO 更嚴格","PGIs' more flexible rules allow a very wide range of styles and quality levels.":"PGI 較彈性的規定容許非常廣泛的風格和品質等級。","PGIs cover wide areas with looser rules than PDOs, giving producers more freedom. Some use that freedom to make outstanding wines sold at a premium. Nothing requires a single grape variety.":"PGI 涵蓋廣大區域，規定比 PDO 寬鬆，給予生產者更多自由。有些生產者利用這份自由釀出以高價出售的傑出酒款。沒有任何規定要求使用單一品種。","Which statement about the term 'Old Vine' / vieilles vignes is correct?":"關於「Old Vine」／vieilles vignes 這個術語，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","It is not legally defined, so its use can be disputed":"它沒有法律定義，所以其使用可能引起爭議","It means vines at least 50 years old under EU law":"根據歐盟法律，它代表至少 50 年樹齡的葡萄樹","It may be used only on PDO wines":"它只能用在 PDO 葡萄酒上","It guarantees a sweet wine, because old vines give sweeter grapes":"它保證是甜酒，因為老藤結的葡萄比較甜","'Old vines' has no legal definition, so there can be disagreement over its use.":"「老藤」沒有法律定義，所以其使用可能有爭議。","Old vines give fewer grapes with more concentrated, complex flavours, hence their prestige. But no law sets a minimum age or limits the term to certain categories. It is about yield and concentration, not sweetness.":"老藤結的葡萄較少，風味更濃縮、更複雜，因此享有聲望。但沒有法律規定最低樹齡，也沒有把這個術語限制在特定類別。它關乎的是產量和濃縮度，而不是甜度。","What does the vintage on a label refer to?":"酒標上的年份指的是什麼？","The year the grapes were harvested":"葡萄採收的年份","The year the wine was bottled":"葡萄酒裝瓶的年份","The year the wine went on sale":"葡萄酒上市的年份","The year the vines that made the wine were planted":"釀酒的葡萄樹種植的年份","The vintage is the year of harvest.":"年份就是採收的年份。","Bottling and release can happen months or years after harvest. The vines' planting year is never shown as the vintage. Knowing the vintage helps you judge the wine's age and whether it is at its best.":"裝瓶和上市可能在採收後數月或數年才進行。葡萄樹的種植年份從不會標示為年份。了解年份有助於判斷酒的年齡，以及它是否處於最佳狀態。","Why is the vintage especially useful for expensive wines from prestigious regions with variable weather?":"對於來自天氣多變的知名產區的昂貴葡萄酒，為什麼年份特別有用？","Each year's weather can greatly affect grape quality":"每年的天氣可能大幅影響葡萄品質","It shows which grape was used":"它顯示使用了哪個品種","It reveals whether the wine is organic":"它透露這款酒是否有機","It proves the wine always has the same style, whatever the year's weather":"它證明無論當年天氣如何，酒的風格總是一樣","Where weather varies a lot year to year, the vintage helps predict style and quality.":"在天氣年年差異很大的地方，年份有助於預測風格和品質。","A cool or rainy year can produce a wine different from what you expect. Knowing it helps you decide if the price is justified and when to drink the wine. The last option says the opposite: variability is exactly why the vintage matters.":"涼爽或多雨的年份釀出的酒可能和你預期的不同。了解這一點有助於判斷價格是否合理，以及何時飲用。最後一個選項說的正好相反：正是因為多變，年份才重要。","A customer wants a dry white and points to an Australian bottle labelled 'Botrytis Semillon'. What should you tell them?":"一位顧客想要不甜的白酒，指著一瓶標示「Botrytis Semillon」的澳洲酒。你應該怎麼告訴他？","That it is almost certainly a sweet wine":"這幾乎可以肯定是一款甜酒","That it is a light, dry white":"這是一款輕盈、不甜的白酒","That it is a red, because Semillon is a black grape":"這是紅酒，因為榭密雍是黑葡萄","That it was ruined by a vineyard disease and should be avoided completely":"它被葡萄園的病害毀了，應該完全避開","Noble-rot grapes are highly concentrated in sugar and nearly always make sweet wines.":"貴腐葡萄的糖分高度濃縮，幾乎都用來釀甜酒。","Semillon is a white grape; outside the EU, varietal labelling is common. Here the Botrytis is beneficial: it is noble rot, which concentrates sugars and acids. For a dry white, suggest a different bottle.":"榭密雍是白葡萄；在歐盟以外，以品種標示很常見。這裡的貴腐菌是有益的：它就是貴腐，會濃縮糖和酸。想要不甜的白酒，就建議另一瓶吧。","What does 'Icewine' or 'Eiswein' on a label tell you about the harvest?":"酒標上的「Icewine」或「Eiswein」告訴你什麼採收資訊？","The grapes were left to freeze on the vine before picking":"葡萄在採收前留在樹上結冰","The grapes were frozen in the winery after harvest":"葡萄在採收後於酒廠冷凍","The wine is meant to be served over ice":"這款酒應該加冰塊飲用","The grapes were affected by noble rot in a very cold region":"葡萄在非常寒冷的產區受到貴腐菌感染","Icewine/Eiswein means grapes frozen naturally on the vine and pressed while still frozen.":"Icewine/Eiswein 是指葡萄在樹上自然結冰，並在結冰狀態下壓榨。","The ice stays in the press and the juice is rich in sugar and acid, usually for sweet wines. Freezing must happen in the vineyard, not the winery. Noble rot is a different concentration method, labelled as Botrytis or Noble Rot.":"冰留在壓榨機裡，果汁富含糖和酸，通常用來釀甜酒。結冰必須發生在葡萄園，而不是酒廠。貴腐是另一種濃縮方法，標示為 Botrytis 或 Noble Rot。","Compared with a wine from a normal harvest, what can you expect from a 'Late Harvest' wine of the same grape?":"與正常採收的酒相比，同一品種的「Late Harvest」葡萄酒可以預期有什麼不同？","More body and more concentration":"酒體更飽滿、更濃縮","Less alcohol and more acidity":"酒精較低、酸度較高","Greener, more herbaceous flavours":"風味更青澀、更有草本氣息","Exactly the same style, since only the bottling date matters":"風格完全相同，因為只有裝瓶日期才重要","Later-picked grapes are riper and sweeter, giving fuller-bodied, more concentrated wines.":"較晚採收的葡萄更成熟、更甜，釀出酒體更飽滿、更濃縮的酒。","Late harvest brings riper flavours and more sugar, not green notes. The wine can still be dry, off-dry, medium or sweet. Lower alcohol and higher acidity are typical of grapes picked early.":"晚收帶來更成熟的風味和更多糖分，而不是青澀的氣息。這款酒仍然可以是不甜、微甜、半甜或甜。酒精較低、酸度較高是早採葡萄的典型特徵。","Which microorganisms carry out alcoholic fermentation?":"哪一種微生物進行酒精發酵？","Bacteria":"細菌","Moulds":"黴菌","Yeast feed on the sugars in the juice and turn them into alcohol.":"酵母以果汁中的糖為食，把糖轉化為酒精。","Alcoholic fermentation is the one process common to all wines, and it is carried out by yeast. Bacteria, on the other hand, are responsible for malolactic conversion, which happens afterwards and lowers acidity. Moulds and enzymes are not what produce the alcohol: mixing them up with yeast is a common exam mistake.":"酒精發酵是所有葡萄酒共有的唯一過程，由酵母進行。相對地，細菌負責乳酸轉化，它發生在之後並降低酸度。製造酒精的不是黴菌或酵素：把它們和酵母搞混是考試中常見的錯誤。","Apart from alcohol, what do yeast produce during fermentation?":"除了酒精，酵母在發酵過程中還產生什麼？","Carbon dioxide and heat":"二氧化碳和熱","Oxygen and acidity":"氧氣和酸","Sugar and water":"糖和水","Fermentation turns sugar into alcohol, CO2 and heat.":"發酵把糖轉化為酒精、CO2 和熱。","As they consume sugar, yeast release alcohol, carbon dioxide and heat. For still wines the CO2 usually escapes into the air, while the heat must be controlled because temperature affects style. Colour and tannin are not made by yeast: they are extracted from the skins of black grapes, and the heat of fermentation helps that extraction.":"酵母消耗糖時，會釋放酒精、二氧化碳和熱。釀造靜態酒時，CO2 通常散逸到空氣中，而熱必須加以控制，因為溫度會影響風格。顏色和單寧不是酵母製造的：它們是從黑葡萄的果皮萃取出來的，發酵的熱有助於萃取。","What mainly determines the alcohol level of a dry wine?":"主要是什麼決定了不甜葡萄酒的酒精濃度？","The amount of sugar in the grapes":"葡萄中的糖量","The type of vessel used":"使用的容器類型","The length of storage":"儲存的時間長短","The amount of tannin in the skins":"果皮中的單寧量","The more sugar in the grapes, the more alcohol the yeast can make.":"葡萄中的糖越多，酵母能產生的酒精就越多。","In a dry wine the yeast use up all the available sugar, so the final alcohol depends on how much sugar there was at the start, in other words on grape ripeness. That is why warm-climate wines tend to be higher in alcohol. Vessels, storage time and tannins affect other aspects of style, but not how much alcohol is produced.":"在不甜的葡萄酒中，酵母會把所有可用的糖消耗殆盡，所以最終的酒精濃度取決於一開始有多少糖，也就是葡萄的成熟度。這就是為什麼溫暖氣候的葡萄酒酒精濃度往往較高。容器、儲存時間和單寧會影響風格的其他方面，但不影響產生多少酒精。","What is the typical alcohol range of most dry wines?":"大多數不甜葡萄酒的典型酒精濃度範圍是多少？","About 11.5–16% abv":"約 11.5–16% abv","About 5–9% abv":"約 5–9% abv","About 15–20% abv":"約 15–20% abv","About 18–22% abv":"約 18–22% abv","Most dry wines sit between about 11.5% and 16% abv.":"大多數不甜葡萄酒的酒精濃度約在 11.5% 到 16% abv 之間。","The alcohol level of dry wines depends on grape sugar and usually falls between 11.5% and 16% abv. The 15–20% abv range belongs to fortified wines, where alcohol is added to stop fermentation. Very low levels, under 10%, are not typical of dry wines, because they suggest that not all the sugar has been converted.":"不甜葡萄酒的酒精濃度取決於葡萄的糖分，通常介於 11.5% 到 16% abv 之間。15–20% abv 的範圍屬於加烈酒，它們是添加酒精來中止發酵的。低於 10% 的極低酒精濃度不是不甜葡萄酒的典型特徵，因為這表示並非所有的糖都被轉化了。","In white winemaking, when does pressing usually take place?":"釀造白酒時，壓榨通常在什麼時候進行？","Before alcoholic fermentation":"酒精發酵之前","After alcoholic fermentation":"酒精發酵之後","During oak maturation":"橡木桶熟成期間","Just before bottling":"就在裝瓶前","For whites, grapes are crushed and pressed before fermenting, without skins.":"釀造白酒時，葡萄在發酵前破皮和壓榨，不帶果皮發酵。","The typical order for a white is crushing, pressing, fermentation, storage or maturation, packaging. The juice ferments apart from the skins, which are usually discarded, because colour and tannin are not wanted. For reds it is the opposite: pressing comes after fermentation, because the skins must stay in contact with the fermenting juice.":"白酒的典型順序是破皮、壓榨、發酵、儲存或熟成、包裝。果汁與果皮分開發酵，果皮通常被丟棄，因為不需要顏色和單寧。紅酒則相反：壓榨在發酵之後，因為果皮必須與發酵中的果汁保持接觸。","What is the typical order for a dry red wine?":"不甜紅酒的典型順序是什麼？","Draining, crushing, fermentation, pressing":"排汁、破皮、發酵、壓榨","In reds the skins ferment with the juice; draining and pressing come afterwards.":"釀造紅酒時，果皮與果汁一起發酵；排汁和壓榨在之後進行。","A red must be made from black grapes, and the skins must stay in the juice during fermentation to give colour and tannin. Only when fermentation is finished is the wine drained off the skins, and the wine left in them is recovered by pressing. Storage or maturation and finally packaging follow.":"紅酒必須用黑葡萄釀造，而且發酵期間果皮必須留在果汁中，以帶來顏色和單寧。只有在發酵結束後，才把酒從果皮中排出，留在果皮中的酒則透過壓榨回收。接著是儲存或熟成，最後是包裝。","Why can white wine be made from black grapes?":"為什麼可以用黑葡萄釀造白酒？","The colour is found only in the skin":"顏色只存在於果皮中","The colour disappears during fermentation":"顏色在發酵過程中消失","The colour is found only in the seeds":"顏色只存在於葡萄籽中","The colour is removed by oak":"顏色被橡木桶去除","Black grape pulp is clear, so gentle pressing keeps the juice colourless.":"黑葡萄的果肉是透明的，所以輕柔壓榨能讓果汁保持無色。","In black grapes the coloured pigments are found only in the skin, not the pulp. If the grapes are pressed very gently, the juice comes out almost colourless and, fermented away from the skins, makes a white wine. For a red, by contrast, the skins must take part in fermentation precisely to release their colour.":"黑葡萄的色素只存在於果皮，不在果肉。如果非常輕柔地壓榨葡萄，流出的果汁幾乎無色，與果皮分開發酵後就成了白酒。相反地，釀造紅酒時，果皮必須參與發酵，正是為了釋放顏色。","In the short maceration method for rosé, when are the skins removed?":"以短時間浸皮法釀造粉紅酒時，果皮在什麼時候移除？","After several weeks of fermentation":"發酵數週之後","Only at bottling":"直到裝瓶時","The skins stay in contact for just a few hours, enough for a light colour.":"果皮只接觸幾個小時，足以帶來淡淡的顏色。","With short maceration, black grapes are used and the process starts like a red, but the fermenting juice is drained off the skins after a few hours. The brief contact gives a pink colour and little tannin. Fermentation then continues without the skins, at the cooler temperatures used for whites, and rosés rarely see oak.":"短時間浸皮法使用黑葡萄，一開始像釀紅酒一樣，但幾個小時後就把發酵中的果汁從果皮中排出。短暫的接觸帶來粉紅色和少量單寧。之後發酵在沒有果皮的情況下繼續進行，溫度與白酒一樣較低，而粉紅酒很少經過橡木桶。","Which rosé method is not permitted in many parts of Europe?":"哪一種粉紅酒釀法在歐洲許多地方不被允許？","Blending red wine with white wine":"把紅酒和白酒混合","Short maceration of black grapes":"黑葡萄短時間浸皮","Fermenting at low temperature":"低溫發酵","Using stainless steel tanks":"使用不鏽鋼槽","Rosé made by blending red and white is banned in many European regions.":"把紅酒和白酒混合釀成的粉紅酒，在歐洲許多產區是禁止的。","The two most common rosé methods are short maceration and blending. In blending, a red wine is mixed with a white wine to achieve the pink colour. It is a simple technique, but it is not permitted in many parts of Europe. Short maceration, by contrast, is allowed and widely used.":"最常見的兩種粉紅酒釀法是短時間浸皮法和混合法。混合法是把紅酒和白酒混合，得到粉紅色。這是一種簡單的技術，但在歐洲許多地方不被允許。相反地，短時間浸皮法是允許的，而且廣泛使用。","Why are red wines fermented at higher temperatures than whites?":"為什麼紅酒的發酵溫度比白酒高？","To extract colour and tannin from the skins":"為了從果皮萃取顏色和單寧","To preserve delicate fruity aromas":"為了保留細緻的果香","To increase the wine's acidity":"為了提高酒的酸度","To stop the yeast early":"為了提早讓酵母停止作用","Heat helps extract colour and tannin from the skins.":"熱有助於從果皮萃取顏色和單寧。","Reds ferment at roughly 20–32°C, whites at 12–22°C. The higher temperatures allow reds to extract colour and tannin from the skins, which are essential to their style. Whites, which ferment without skins, benefit instead from cooler temperatures, which bring out fruity aromas.":"紅酒的發酵溫度約為 20–32°C，白酒則為 12–22°C。較高的溫度讓紅酒能從果皮萃取顏色和單寧，這對紅酒的風格不可或缺。不帶果皮發酵的白酒，則受益於較低的溫度，能帶出果香。","Which temperature range is typical for fermenting white wines?":"白酒典型的發酵溫度範圍是多少？","12–22°C (54–72°F)":"12–22°C（54–72°F）","20–32°C (68–90°F)":"20–32°C（68–90°F）","2–8°C (36–46°F)":"2–8°C（36–46°F）","30–40°C (86–104°F)":"30–40°C（86–104°F）","Whites ferment at 12–22°C, cooler than reds.":"白酒在 12–22°C 發酵，比紅酒低。","Whites ferment at roughly 12–22°C. At the cooler end of that range, fermentation can produce pronounced fruity aromas, prized in many fresh whites. The 20–32°C range belongs to reds, which need heat to extract colour and tannin. Short-maceration rosés, once drained, ferment at temperatures similar to whites.":"白酒的發酵溫度約為 12–22°C。在這個範圍的低溫端發酵，可以產生濃郁的果香，這在許多清爽的白酒中備受珍視。20–32°C 的範圍屬於紅酒，紅酒需要熱來萃取顏色和單寧。短時間浸皮的粉紅酒在排汁後，以類似白酒的溫度發酵。","A white wine fermented at a very cool temperature is most likely to show...":"一款在非常低溫下發酵的白酒，最可能表現出……","Pronounced fruity aromas":"濃郁的果香","High tannin":"高單寧","Nut and caramel aromas":"堅果和焦糖香氣","A deep amber colour":"深琥珀色","Cool white fermentations can produce pronounced fruity aromas.":"低溫發酵的白酒可以產生濃郁的果香。","At the cool end of the white range, around 12°C, fermentation can bring out pronounced fruity aromas. Nut and caramel come from contact with oxygen during barrel maturation, while an amber colour is a sign of age. High tannin does not apply to whites, which ferment without their skins.":"在白酒溫度範圍的低溫端，約 12°C 左右，發酵可以帶出濃郁的果香。堅果和焦糖來自橡木桶熟成期間與氧氣的接觸，而琥珀色則是陳年的跡象。高單寧不適用於白酒，因為白酒不帶果皮發酵。","What is the \"cap\" in red winemaking?":"紅酒釀造中的「酒帽」是什麼？","The layer of skins that floats to the top":"浮到頂部的果皮層","The layer of dead yeast at the bottom":"底部的死酵母層","The lid used to close the vessel":"用來封住容器的蓋子","The CO2 foam on top of the wine":"酒液表面的 CO2 泡沫","The skins float and form a thick layer called the cap.":"果皮浮起，形成一層稱為酒帽的厚層。","During red fermentation the skins rise and form the cap. Left undisturbed it gives up little colour and tannin, so it must be mixed often with the liquid by punching down or pumping over. The layer of dead yeast at the bottom, on the other hand, is called the lees and mostly matters in white winemaking.":"紅酒發酵期間，果皮上浮形成酒帽。如果不加處理，酒帽釋放的顏色和單寧很少，所以必須經常透過壓帽或淋汁讓它與液體混合。另一方面，底部的死酵母層稱為酒渣，主要在白酒釀造中發揮作用。","In which technique is liquid from the bottom of the vessel sprayed over the cap?":"哪一種技術是把容器底部的液體噴淋到酒帽上？","In pumping over, liquid is pumped through a hose and sprayed over the cap.":"淋汁是用管子抽取液體，噴淋到酒帽上。","Pumping over and punching down both mix skins and liquid to extract colour and tannin. In pumping over, liquid is drawn from the bottom of the vessel and sprayed over the cap; in punching down, a plunger pushes the cap down into the liquid. Draining and pressing take place once fermentation has finished.":"淋汁和壓帽都是讓果皮與液體混合，以萃取顏色和單寧。淋汁是從容器底部抽取液體，噴淋到酒帽上；壓帽則是用壓棒把酒帽壓入液體中。排汁和壓榨在發酵結束後進行。","In a cool vintage, why might a winemaker increase the sugar in the juice?":"在涼爽的年份，釀酒師為什麼可能提高果汁中的糖分？","To avoid a wine low in alcohol and body":"避免酒的酒精和酒體不足","To make the wine sweet":"讓酒變甜","To lower the acidity":"降低酸度","To extract more tannin":"萃取更多單寧","More sugar to ferment means more alcohol and more body.":"可發酵的糖越多，酒精和酒體就越多。","In cool climates or vintages the grapes may not ripen fully and may lack sugar, giving a wine low in alcohol and lacking body. Raising the sugar in the juice gives the yeast more to convert, so the finished wine has more alcohol. The added sugar is fermented, so the wine stays dry.":"在涼爽的氣候或年份，葡萄可能無法完全成熟、糖分不足，釀出的酒酒精低、酒體單薄。提高果汁中的糖分，讓酵母有更多可轉化的糖，成品酒的酒精就更高。添加的糖會被發酵掉，所以酒仍然是不甜的。","In a warm climate, which adjustment is most likely?":"在溫暖氣候中，最可能進行哪一種調整？","Adding acid":"加酸","Neutralising acid":"中和酸","Adding sugar":"加糖","Adding tannin":"添加單寧","In warm climates acidity drops sharply, leaving the wine unbalanced.":"在溫暖氣候中，酸度會大幅下降，讓酒失去平衡。","During ripening in a warm climate, grape acidity can fall very low. A wine with too little acidity would be unbalanced, so the winemaker may add acid in the winery. Neutralising acid and raising sugar are, by contrast, typical adjustments for cool climates, where grapes ripen with more acid and less sugar.":"在溫暖氣候中成熟時，葡萄的酸度可能降得非常低。酸度太低的酒會失去平衡，所以釀酒師可能在酒廠中加酸。相反地，中和酸和提高糖分是涼爽氣候的典型調整，因為那裡的葡萄成熟時酸較多、糖較少。","How does Tokaji Aszú get its sweetness?":"Tokaji Aszú 的甜味是怎麼來的？","From grapes with concentrated sugars":"來自糖分濃縮的葡萄","By adding alcohol":"添加酒精","By filtering out the yeast":"把酵母過濾掉","By adding juice to a dry wine":"在不甜的酒中加入果汁","The sugar is so concentrated that the yeast cannot consume it all.":"糖分濃縮到酵母無法全部消耗。","Tokaji Aszú from Hungary is made from grapes with highly concentrated sugars. When the juice is that sugary, the yeast cannot ferment it all, and fermentation stops with residual sugar left over. Adding alcohol is typical of Port, and filtering out yeast of White Zinfandel.":"匈牙利的 Tokaji Aszú 是用糖分高度濃縮的葡萄釀造的。當果汁這麼甜時，酵母無法把糖全部發酵完，發酵停止時就留下殘糖。添加酒精是 Port 的典型做法，過濾酵母則是 White Zinfandel 的做法。","Which sweet wine is made by removing the yeast with very fine filters?":"哪一種甜酒是用非常細的過濾器去除酵母釀成的？","Californian White Zinfandel uses filters that catch the yeast.":"加州的 White Zinfandel 使用能攔住酵母的過濾器。","Removing yeast from fermenting juice requires extremely sophisticated filters with holes small enough to catch them. Without yeast, fermentation stops and residual sugar remains: this is how White Zinfandel from California is made. Port is made by adding alcohol, while Tokaji Aszú and icewine start from grapes with concentrated sugars.":"要從發酵中的果汁去除酵母，需要極為精密、孔洞小到能攔住酵母的過濾器。沒有了酵母，發酵就停止，留下殘糖：加州的 White Zinfandel 就是這樣釀成的。Port 是添加酒精釀成的，而 Tokaji Aszú 和冰酒則是從糖分濃縮的葡萄開始。","Why is a fortified wine such as Port in no danger of fermenting again?":"為什麼像 Port 這樣的加烈酒沒有再次發酵的風險？","Alcohol at 15–20% abv kills the yeast":"15–20% abv 的酒精會殺死酵母","All the sugar has been used up":"所有的糖都已經用完了","The wine is filtered several times":"酒經過多次過濾","The wine is kept at a low temperature":"酒保存在低溫下","The added alcohol takes the wine to a level that kills yeast.":"添加的酒精讓酒達到足以殺死酵母的濃度。","Fortification adds alcohol to the fermenting juice, raising it to 15–20% abv. At this level the yeast die before they have used all the sugar, which stays in the wine as sweetness. The high alcohol also stops fermentation from restarting later, which is why Port is stable even though it is sweet.":"加烈是在發酵中的果汁裡添加酒精，把濃度提高到 15–20% abv。在這個濃度下，酵母在用完所有糖之前就死亡了，剩下的糖以甜味的形式留在酒中。高酒精也能防止日後重新發酵，這就是為什麼 Port 雖然是甜的，卻很穩定。","What is the main advantage of adding sweetness to a dry wine?":"在不甜的酒中添加甜味，主要的好處是什麼？","Precise control of the sweetness level":"精準控制甜度","A much higher alcohol level":"酒精濃度大幅提高","Softer tannins":"單寧更柔和","More intense oak flavours":"橡木桶風味更濃郁","Adding sweetness after fermentation lets the final sugar be set exactly.":"在發酵後添加甜味，可以準確設定最終的糖分。","This technique is widely used for red, white and rosé wines precisely because the winemaker can control sweetness accurately. The added sugar always comes from grapes: unfermented juice, very sweet concentrated juice, or a sweet wine blended with the dry one. It does not affect tannins or oak flavours.":"這項技術廣泛用於紅酒、白酒和粉紅酒，正是因為釀酒師可以精準控制甜度。添加的糖一定來自葡萄：未發酵的葡萄汁、非常甜的濃縮葡萄汁，或與不甜的酒混合的甜酒。它不會影響單寧或橡木桶風味。","What does crushing involve?":"破皮是指什麼？","Splitting the skins to release some of the juice":"把果皮弄破，釋放出一部分果汁","Squeezing the grapes to extract as much liquid as possible":"擠壓葡萄，盡可能取出最多液體","Separating the wine from the lees after fermentation":"發酵後把酒和酒渣分開","Pushing the cap of skins into the liquid with a plunger during red fermentation":"紅酒發酵期間用壓棒把果皮形成的酒帽壓入液體","Crushing means splitting the grape skins so some juice comes out.":"破皮是把葡萄果皮弄破，讓一部分果汁流出。","Squeezing hard is pressing, done in a press. Pushing the cap into the liquid is punching down, used for reds. Crushing is the first step for both white and red wines.":"用力擠壓是壓榨，在壓榨機中進行。把酒帽壓入液體是壓帽，用於紅酒。破皮是白酒和紅酒共同的第一步。","Which statement about pressing is correct?":"關於壓榨，下列哪一項敘述是正確的？","It can take place before or after fermentation":"它可以在發酵之前或之後進行","It always happens after fermentation":"它總是在發酵之後進行","It always happens before crushing":"它總是在破皮之前進行","It is only used for sweet wines from frozen or noble-rot grapes":"它只用於以冰凍或貴腐葡萄釀造的甜酒","White wines are pressed before fermentation, red wines after it.":"白酒在發酵前壓榨，紅酒在發酵後壓榨。","Pressing squeezes crushed grapes to get out as much liquid as possible. For whites it separates juice from skins before fermentation; for reds it recovers the wine left in the skins after draining. It always follows crushing, never precedes it.":"壓榨是擠壓破皮後的葡萄，盡可能取出最多液體。對白酒來說，它在發酵前把果汁與果皮分開；對紅酒來說，它在排汁後回收留在果皮中的酒。壓榨總是在破皮之後，從不在之前。","When making a still wine, what happens to the carbon dioxide produced by the yeast?":"釀造靜態酒時，酵母產生的二氧化碳會怎樣？","It escapes into the atmosphere":"散逸到大氣中","It stays dissolved and makes the wine fizzy":"保持溶解，讓酒有氣泡","It turns into alcohol":"轉化為酒精","It is reabsorbed by the skins and deepens a red wine's colour":"被果皮重新吸收，加深紅酒的顏色","For still wines, fermentation CO2 is allowed to escape into the air.":"釀造靜態酒時，發酵產生的 CO2 會散逸到空氣中。","Yeast turn sugar into alcohol, CO2 and heat; CO2 is a product, it does not become alcohol. If it were trapped the wine would be fizzy. Red colour comes from the skins, helped by fermentation heat, not from CO2.":"酵母把糖轉化為酒精、CO2 和熱；CO2 是產物，不會變成酒精。如果把它封住，酒就會有氣泡。紅酒的顏色來自果皮，並藉助發酵的熱，而不是來自 CO2。","When does alcoholic fermentation usually stop naturally?":"酒精發酵通常在什麼時候自然停止？","When the yeast have eaten all the sugar":"當酵母把糖全部吃完時","After exactly one week":"剛好一週之後","When the wine reaches 5% abv":"當酒達到 5% abv 時","When the winemaker adds concentrated grape sugar to block the yeast":"當釀酒師加入濃縮葡萄糖來阻止酵母時","Fermentation typically ends on its own once no sugar is left, giving a dry wine.":"發酵通常在沒有糖剩下時自行結束，得到不甜的酒。","The final strength depends on the starting sugar: most dry wines are 11.5–16% abv. There is no fixed duration. Sweet wines use other techniques, such as highly concentrated grapes, filtration or adding alcohol.":"最終的酒精濃度取決於起始糖分：大多數不甜葡萄酒為 11.5–16% abv。發酵沒有固定的時間長度。甜酒則使用其他技術，例如高度濃縮的葡萄、過濾或添加酒精。","For most wines, how long is the storage period before bottling, and with what effect?":"對大多數葡萄酒來說，裝瓶前的儲存期有多長？效果如何？","Less than a year, with flavours changing little if at all":"不到一年，風味幾乎沒有變化","Several years in oak, with strong tertiary development":"在橡木桶中數年，發展出強烈的三級香氣","A few days, during which the wine gets sweeter":"幾天，期間酒會變甜","At least ten years in bottle, because every wine improves with time":"至少在瓶中十年，因為每一款酒都會隨時間變好","Most wine is stored for under a year, sometimes only months, and changes very little.":"大多數葡萄酒儲存不到一年，有時只有幾個月，變化非常小。","Only some wines are kept for long; this is called maturation, with flavours moving from primary to tertiary. Most wines do not improve in bottle and are best drunk young. Storage adds no sugar.":"只有部分葡萄酒會長期存放；這稱為熟成，風味從一級香氣轉向三級香氣。大多數葡萄酒不會在瓶中變好，最好趁年輕飲用。儲存不會增加糖分。","What happens to a wine during extended maturation?":"長時間熟成期間，葡萄酒會發生什麼？","Flavours move from primary to tertiary and tannins become more integrated":"風味從一級轉向三級，單寧變得更融合","The wine regains the flavours of fresh grape juice":"酒重新獲得新鮮葡萄汁的風味","The alcohol rises by a few degrees":"酒精上升幾度","Tannins get harsher and red wines keep getting deeper in colour":"單寧變得更粗糙，紅酒的顏色越來越深","Maturation brings tertiary flavours and makes structure, such as tannin, more integrated.":"熟成帶來三級風味，並讓單寧等結構更融合。","Maturation usually takes place in oak, which can also add secondary flavours. Fruit loses freshness and never returns to fresh juice character. Tannins soften and red colour tends to fade; alcohol does not rise.":"熟成通常在橡木桶中進行，橡木桶也可能增添二級風味。果味失去新鮮感，再也不會回到新鮮果汁的特徵。單寧變柔和，紅酒的顏色傾向變淡；酒精不會上升。","What is still the most popular form of wine packaging?":"至今最受歡迎的葡萄酒包裝形式是什麼？"});(window.TWG_I18N_F=window.TWG_I18N_F||{})["zh-hant/l2"]=1;
